itle-name-text">Find Correct SSL Service for mychainlink.ca Using Manage</s=
pan></div> <!----> <div data-v-064cc47f=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-title-contai=
ner-extra"> <svg data-v-064cc47f=3D"" xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" =
xmlns:xlink=3D"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden=3D"true" role=3D"i=
mg" class=3D"iconify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width=3D"1em" he=
ight=3D"1em" viewBox=3D"0 0 1024 1024" name=3D"Right_b"><path d=3D"M681.000=
96 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864=
 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.8=
64 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill=3D"currentColor"><=
/path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" cla=
ss=3D"toolcall-content"><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top=
" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-cont=
ainer" style=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=
=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D=
"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The Connections panel s=
hows:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">mychai=
nlink.ca (EXTERNAL DOMAIN) connected to: Hyperlift Micro (ONLINE), Spacemai=
l Pro (ONLINE), Thunderbolt Free (ONLINE), SSL FreeSSL (ONLINE).</div></li>=
</ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So there's an SSL connection "Fr=
eeSSL" that is ONLINE. Hmm =E2=80=94 so SSL is connected and online, yet th=
e browser gets a common-name mismatch.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D=
"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 the connection panel shows mychainlink.ca connected t=
o Hyperlift Micro, Spacemail, Thunderbolt, AND FreeSSL. All ONLINE. But the=
 app card said "Connection issue."</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">Interesting: Thunderbolt Free =E2=80=94 Thunderbolt is Spaceship's web h=
osting (cPanel-ish). FreeSSL is likely attached to the Thunderbolt hosting,=
 not Hyperlift! So mychainlink.ca's DNS might still be pointing at the OLD =
hosting (Thunderbolt?) or the domain connection list includes multiple serv=
ices but DNS A record still points somewhere serving the wrong cert (e.g., =
the Thunderbolt server's default/FreeSSL cert for a different domain, or Gi=
tHub Pages still).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The "Connecti=
on issue" badge on the Hyperlift card suggests Hyperlift knows the domain i=
sn't properly routed to it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Diag=
nosis paths:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>The DNS A record for mychainlink.ca needs to point at Hyperlift's IP. Sinc=
e the domain was on GitHub Pages, the A records point at GitHub Pages IPs (=
185.199.x.x). Until she updates DNS (in Spaceship's DNS settings) to Hyperl=
ift's provided IP, requests may hit GitHub Pages (which now serves... hmm, =
but GitHub Pages would serve HER cert? GitHub Pages certs are per-site; if =
the site is still "live" on Pages, the cert would be valid for mychainlink.=
ca. Unless she disabled Pages or the CNAME was removed =E2=86=92 GitHub ser=
ves cert for github.io =E2=86=92 COMMON_NAME_INVALID!)</div></li></ol><div =
class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">That's plausible: if GitHub Pages got disc=
onnected (custom domain removed, or repo renamed), hitting GitHub Pages IPs=
 with mychainlink.ca SNI returns a *.github.io cert =E2=86=92 ERR_CERT_COMM=
ON_NAME_INVALID. Exactly matches!</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
">Earlier at 3:45am the site worked (I fetched it). Then around 4:30 it bro=
ke =E2=80=94 maybe GitHub Pages got disabled mid-move (she might have turne=
d it off, or the "Welcome to Hyperlift" placeholder + DNS moved to Hyperlif=
t, but Hyperlift's cert not ready =E2=86=92 default cert mismatch).</div><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So resolution: check where DNS points a=
nd either (a) point A record to Hyperlift's IP, or (b) if DNS already point=
s to Hyperlift, the FreeSSL cert needs to be issued for mychainlink.ca =E2=
=80=94 "SSL FreeSSL ONLINE" though. But which service is FreeSSL attached t=
o? If attached to Thunderbolt hosting while domain routes to Hyperlift, the=
 wrong cert gets served.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Next st=
ep: click "Manage" on the mychainlink.ca EXTERNAL DOMAIN row =E2=80=94 that=
 should show DNS records / routing details. One instruction: click the Mana=
ge button next to mychainlink.ca (with the little door/exit icon) and scree=
nshot. That should reveal nameservers/DNS/A record or the connection status=
 detail.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Given her exhaustion (4=
:48am), keep it to one click + screenshot.</div></div></div></div></div> <d=
iv class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true">=
</div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"=
></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div=
 data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"=
><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-c=
ontainer"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">This panel is super telling, boss. Look at it: your domai=
n is "connected" to FOUR services =E2=80=94 Hyperlift Micro, Spacemail, <st=
rong>Thunderbolt</strong> (Spaceship's old-school web hosting), and a free =
SSL. All green "ONLINE." But your Hyperlift card still screams =E2=9A=A0 Co=
nnection issue.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Here's my read: =
the domain's address book (DNS) is still pointing at the <em>old</em> neigh=
bourhood =E2=80=94 probably still saying "GitHub Pages" from before =E2=80=
=94 so when anyone knocks on mychainlink.ca, they get a mismatched certific=
ate from a server that isn't yours anymore. The FreeSSL cert is sitting on =
the wrong doorstep.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let's confir=
m it:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Step 1:</strong> I=
n that same panel, click the <strong>"Manage"</strong> button next to <stro=
ng>mychainlink.ca</strong> (the row that says EXTERNAL DOMAIN =E2=80=94 it =
has a little door icon).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">That op=
ens the domain's connection/DNS details. Screenshot me whatever comes up =
=E2=80=94 the address book will be right there, and then I'll tell you the =
exact record to change =F0=9F=93=96=F0=9F=94=8D</div></div></div></div> <di=
v data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-0a722276=
=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> =
