=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-content"><div class=3D"scroll-=
edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div data-v-b900=
66f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><di=
v data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" d=
ata-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div=
 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">She's confused and exhausted (4:57am). Let me piece together what the s=
creenshots show:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto"><strong>Domain Portfolio</strong>: only cleanedbykendal.ca is listed! =
mychainlink.ca is NOT in her Spaceship domain portfolio. That's why it says=
 "EXTERNAL DOMAIN" =E2=80=94 mychainlink.ca is registered elsewhere (probab=
ly Namecheap, GoDaddy, or Cloudflare... earlier note said cleanedbykendal.c=
a is hosted on Spaceship; mychainlink.ca's registrar is unknown =E2=80=94 l=
ikely not Spaceship).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><=
strong>Connection Manager</strong>: mychainlink.ca (EXTERNAL DOMAIN) connec=
ted to Hyperlift Micro (expires Oct 08, 2026), Spacemail Pro, Thunderbolt F=
ree, SSL FreeSSL =E2=80=94 all "ONLINE".</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>URL redirect panel</strong>: shows "Connection is=
sue =E2=80=94 This connection has an issue affecting how your products work=
 together. You can disconnect the products if you no longer need this conne=
ction." =E2=80=94 this is a URL redirect connection (redirect to <a data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"nor=
eferrer nofollow noopener">www.example.com</a> placeholder). Interesting: t=
here's a "URL redirect" connection with an issue =E2=80=94 maybe a leftover=
 redirect pointing somewhere.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">So the actual situation: mychainlink.ca is registered at ANOTHER =
registrar, and its DNS is controlled elsewhere. For Hyperlift + SSL to work=
, the domain's DNS records (A record) must point to Hyperlift's IP, and SSL=
 cert must be issued for mychainlink.ca.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 but earlier (3:43-4:06 AM) the site WORKED on mych=
ainlink.ca through Hyperlift. So DNS was pointing at Hyperlift then. Now ce=
rt mismatch...</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm, let me think=
 again. At 3:45 the placeholder "Welcome to Hyperlift app" showed. At 3:55 =
she added env vars, built, and at 4:06 the deploy completed. At 4:08 I fetc=
hed the site successfully =E2=80=94 full content served by server.js! So DN=
S =E2=86=92 Hyperlift was working with valid SSL at 4:08 (my fetch tool wou=
ld have failed on bad cert).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Bet=
ween 4:08 and 4:40, something changed =E2=86=92 cert mismatch. What could s=
he have done? Looking at the tabs in her screenshots: "My Chain Link - Das.=
.." (dashboard), Supabase, "GitHub=E6=96=87=E4=BB=B6=E6=81=A2=E5=A4=8D - Ki=
mi" (Kimi file recovery in Chinese?? interesting tab), transaction/manageme=
nt tab, Dockerfile tab, My Chain Link.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D=
"auto">Possibly: In the Connections panel, there was a "URL redirect" conne=
ction with the placeholder "<a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=
=3D"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">www.examp=
le.com</a>" =E2=80=94 if she clicked around and saved a URL redirect (redir=
ect mychainlink.ca =E2=86=92 <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=
=3D"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">www.examp=
le.com</a> or something), traffic might now be redirecting/hitting FreeSSL'=
s redirect server with a mismatched cert! The third screenshot shows the UR=
L redirect panel with "Redirect to <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank=
" href=3D"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">www=
.example.com</a>" placeholder and 302 temporary =E2=80=94 and the "Connecti=
on issue" notice on it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">OR the F=
reeSSL cert for Hyperlift hasn't been issued for mychainlink.ca yet, and at=
 4:08 my fetch worked because... hmm, my fetch worked at 4:08. Something ch=
anged after.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also possible: DNS =
for mychainlink.ca is managed at the external registrar, and it still has G=
itHub Pages A records. The Hyperlift "connection" works via Spaceship proxy=
ing? No =E2=80=94 Hyperlift needs A record pointing to it. "EXTERNAL DOMAIN=
" with "No expiration" connected to Hyperlift =E2=80=94 Spaceship's connect=
ion system presumably instructs you to point DNS. If DNS still points at Gi=
tHub Pages, then at 3:45-4:08, how did Hyperlift serve the site? Because Gi=
tHub Pages was still serving (site worked there until Pages disabled or CNA=
ME removed). My fetch at 4:08 showed full app content =E2=80=94 that could =
have come from GitHub Pages (static) OR Hyperlift. Then if Pages got turned=
 off / CNAME deleted (maybe by her clicking around, or by the "URL redirect=
" connection creation which hijacked DNS?), requests now land on a server w=
ith a wrong cert.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Too much specu=
lation. The actionable insight: mychainlink.ca is an EXTERNAL domain =E2=80=
=94 its DNS lives at its registrar (not Spaceship). The fix: point the doma=
in's A record to Hyperlift (Spaceship should show the target IP in the Hype=
rlift Manage panel), and let FreeSSL issue the cert.</div><div class=3D"par=
agraph" dir=3D"auto">Also that "URL redirect" connection with issue =E2=80=
=94 she may have accidentally created a redirect connection (with placehold=
er example.com) =E2=80=94 that could be hijacking traffic! The panel says "=
Set up a free SSL-protected URL redirect to forward traffic from your domai=
n to a destination URL. Redirect to: <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_bla=
nk" href=3D"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">w=
ww.example.com</a>" =E2=80=94 if that's an active connection, mychainlink.c=
a might be redirecting to <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D=
"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">www.example.=
com</a>! That would break everything.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Best next step: in the Connection Manager, find that URL redirect con=
nection and DELETE it (or fix it), and check the Hyperlift Micro Manage pan=
el for the DNS target. But one step at a time =E2=80=94 she's overwhelmed (=
"i dont get it"), exhausted.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Sim=
plest, calmest framing: "Nothing's broken beyond repair =E2=80=94 the domai=
n's address book lives at the company where you BOUGHT mychainlink.ca (not =
Spaceship), and right now it has a leftover detour. We're going to delete o=
ne stray connection, then point the address book at Hyperlift."</div><div c=
lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait, but I shouldn't over-assert. Let me b=
e careful about the URL redirect =E2=80=94 it might just be an empty/unconf=
igured connection showing the issue notice. The notice says "This connectio=
n has an issue... You can disconnect the products if you no longer need thi=
s connection." That notice might relate to the whole connection group, not =
just redirect.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Priority action f=
or her RIGHT NOW (4:57am, fried): honestly, the best move might be: stop fo=
r tonight. The site is deployed and healthy; the domain routing is a DNS pr=
opagation/config issue that support (Alf/Spaceship) can resolve, or we tack=
le fresh tomorrow. But she's in "fix it now" mode. Offer a choice: quick at=
tempt now vs sleep.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Given she sa=
id "i dont get it" =E2=80=94 simplify MASSIVELY. Explain in one analogy, th=
en ONE action.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">My one action: In=
 the Connection Manager, next to the "URL redirect" entry there's a "=E2=8B=
=AE" menu =E2=80=94 disconnect/delete that redirect connection (it points a=
t example.com =E2=80=94 a placeholder =E2=80=94 which is wrong). Then check=
 mychainlink.ca again.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm, but =
is the URL redirect actually active? The screenshot shows the panel to CONF=
IGURE a redirect =E2=80=94 "Redirect to <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_=
blank" href=3D"http://www.example.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener=
">www.example.com</a>" is the placeholder text (grey). The "Connection issu=
e" banner is at top. It might be an unconfigured redirect she clicked into.=
 If it were active with example.com, the site would redirect to example.com=
, not show cert error. So the redirect is probably NOT the cause; it's just=
 an empty connection flagged with an issue.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">The more likely cause: DNS for mychainlink.ca (managed at exter=
nal registrar) doesn't point to Hyperlift; it flapped earlier because GitHu=
b Pages was still answering (DNS still pointed at GitHub). Then something (=
GitHub Pages disabled? CNAME removed? DNS change?) stopped GitHub from answ=
ering =E2=86=92 now the requests go... where? If DNS still points to GitHub=
 IPs and GitHub has no site for it, GitHub serves its own cert =E2=86=92 CO=
MMON_NAME_INVALID. That fits perfectly! And it means the DNS A records at h=
er registrar still point at GitHub Pages.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">But wait =E2=80=94 the "Welcome to Hyperlift" placeholder at 3:45=
 and my successful fetch at 4:08... If DNS pointed at GitHub the whole time=
, the Hyperlift placeholder couldn't have shown. Unless Spaceship's connect=
ion system proxies via their DNS? No... OR mychainlink.ca uses Spaceship DN=
S? No =E2=80=94 domain is external.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">Alternative: DNS was changed to Hyperlift at some point (when she set u=
p the Hyperlift connection on Sep 8!), and GitHub Pages was ALSO still answ=
ering until ~4:30 when propagation completed or GitHub stopped serving. Hmm=
, that timeline could work: DNS changed earlier =E2=86=92 propagation in pr=
ogress =E2=86=92 during propagation some resolvers still gave GitHub IPs (w=
orked, served her site via Pages) =E2=86=92 once fully propagated to Hyperl=
ift's IP =E2=86=92 Hyperlift serves... but then why cert mismatch? Hyperlif=
t's SSL would be FreeSSL for mychainlink.ca =E2=80=94 if issued, fine; mayb=
e FreeSSL issuance failed (domain validation needs DNS at Spaceship? extern=
al domain... FreeSSL might have failed to validate because the domain isn't=
 on Spaceship DNS!). That fits "Connection issue"!</div><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">OK. Enough. Actionable path: she needs to point DNS to H=
yperlift (done?) and get FreeSSL to issue for mychainlink.ca. The "Manage" =
on the SSL FreeSSL row should show cert status. But honestly =E2=80=94 SHE =
needs Spaceship support or Alf at this point; it's their panel's issue stat=
e. There's an "Ask Alf" button right there =E2=80=94 Spaceship's AI assista=
nt.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Recommendation: It's 5am. Th=
e app is deployed and fine; only the domain routing is in limbo. Two option=
s:
A. Quick win attempt: click "Manage" on the SSL FreeSSL row =E2=86=92 see s=
tatus/issue =E2=86=92 screenshot.
B. Ask Alf / Spaceship support: "mychainlink.ca connected to Hyperlift Micr=
o shows connection issue, site serves wrong SSL cert, domain is external" =
=E2=80=94 they can see backend state.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Also the phone test would confirm global DNS state =E2=80=94 her phon=
e is charging.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Decision: give he=
r the SIMPLEST single action: click the "Manage" on SSL FreeSSL row and scr=
eenshot. If it shows an error/issue we can't fix in UI, then Ask Alf with a=
 paste-ready message I write for her.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Keep the message SHORT =E2=80=94 she's fried. Validate feelings: "you=
 don't need to get it =E2=80=94 that's my job."</div></div></div></div></di=
v> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"t=
rue"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"=
true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div=
><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__=
flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markd=
own-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto">You don't need to get it, boss =E2=80=94 that's lite=
rally my job. Here's the whole picture in one sentence: <strong>mychainlink=
.ca was bought at a different company, its address book is over THERE, and =
the address book is still sending people to the old house.</strong> Your ap=
p is fine. The roads are just wrong.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto">It's 5am and your brain has earned a break, so here's the deal =E2=80=
=94 one last click, then we either fix it or hand it to Spaceship's own hel=
per:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Step 1:</strong> In=
 that Connection Manager list, click <strong>"Manage"</strong> next to <str=
ong>SSL FreeSSL</strong> (the green lock row).</div><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">Screenshot me what it says =E2=80=94 it'll show us whether y=
our security certificate was actually issued for mychainlink.ca or if it's =
stuck/erroring. That's the last puzzle piece =F0=9F=A7=A9</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">(And if that panel just shrugs at us, we paste =
a message into their <strong>Ask Alf</strong> chat =E2=80=94 which is right=
 there in the corner =E2=80=94 and let Spaceship's own crew untangle the ex=
ternal-domain routing while you sleep. Nothing about your app is broken. Th=
is is address-book plumbing.)</div></div></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=
=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"to=
olcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></=
