"1em" height=3D"1em" viewBox=3D"0 0 1024 1024" name=3D"Right_b"><path d=3D"=
M681.00096 549.23264a36.864 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.4764=
8a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69=
344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill=3D"current=
Color"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=
=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-content"><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge=
-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"re=
size-container" style=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"=
" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" c=
lass=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D""=
 class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The FreeSSL panel=
 for mychainlink.ca:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">FreeSSL $0.00</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>"tdekmtb SSL ID" (some cert ID)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Renews on Dec 12, 2026</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Connections: 4 products</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">No status showing issued/active, no domain validation info.</div=
></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So the SSL cert exists (an=
 ID, renewal date Dec 12, 2026). But the site serves a mismatched cert. The=
 FreeSSL cert is connected to 4 products (Hyperlift, Spacemail, Thunderbolt=
, +1?).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The cert exists but the =
domain's DNS doesn't route to the server presenting this cert =E2=80=94 or =
the cert was issued for a different common name? Can't tell from here.</div=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Honestly, at this point the cleanest=
 path: hand it to Spaceship's Ask Alf with a precise description, or their =
live support. The issue involves an external domain's DNS pointing (which l=
ives at the other registrar) + Hyperlift routing + SSL =E2=80=94 their supp=
ort can see backend state (connection issue flag).</div><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Also one more diagnostic SHE can do instantly: check whe=
re the domain points. She could open a terminal?? Too technical. The phone =
test (now charged?) tells us if it's global: if phone also shows cert error=
 =E2=86=92 global DNS/cert issue =E2=86=92 Spaceship's problem to fix. That=
's still the key discriminator, and now ~15 min have passed since she plugg=
ed it in.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Two options for next s=
tep:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Phone t=
est (if charged): does Safari load mychainlink.ca?</div></li><li><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">If same error =E2=86=92 Ask Alf with my paste-r=
eady message.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me g=
ive her the Ask Alf message NOW so we skip a round trip: "If your phone sho=
ws the same warning, click Ask Alf and paste this:" with a prewritten suppo=
rt message. That's efficient =E2=80=94 one message, conditional.</div><div =
class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Write the Alf message clearly:</div><div c=
lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">"Hi! My domain mychainlink.ca (registered e=
xternally) is connected to my Hyperlift Micro app 'My Chain Link' (repo myc=
hainlinkCA/Mychainlink). The app builds and deploys fine, but mychainlink.c=
a shows ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID in browsers, and the connection shows =
'Connection issue.' FreeSSL (ID tdekmtb) is connected and shows renewal Dec=
 12 2026. Do I need to update DNS records at my external registrar to point=
 to Hyperlift? What IP/records should the domain have, and is the FreeSSL c=
ertificate correctly issued for mychainlink.ca on the Hyperlift connection?=
"</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Keep my message short: cert ex=
ists, so the plumbing issue is on routing =E2=80=94 hand to Alf. Also remin=
d: don't proceed past warnings; phone check first if convenient.</div></div=
></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom"=
 aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel=
" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!-=
---> <!----></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part =
toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D=
"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown=
"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Okay =E2=80=94 that panel tells me =
the certificate <strong>exists</strong> (it's got an ID and renews Dec 12, =
2026) =E2=9C=85 So your lock was cut. The problem is the mailman: browsers =
are knocking on mychainlink.ca and being sent to a <em>different</em> door =
than the one holding your lock. That's the "Connection issue" flag =E2=80=
=94 and since your domain lives at another company (that's what "EXTERNAL" =
means), the wrong-turn is happening in the address book over there.</div><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">This is officially above our pay grade =
=E2=80=94 Spaceship's own crew can see the backend routing and tell you the=
 exact fix (usually: point the domain's A record at Hyperlift's IP, or re-i=
ssue the cert to the right door).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
"><strong>Final step for tonight:</strong> Click the <strong>"Ask Alf"</str=
ong> button (bottom-left of Spaceship) and paste exactly this:</div><div da=
