a-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-content"><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade=
 scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div data-v-b90066f2=3D""=
 class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-=
b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-901=
9dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-0=
48cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Plot =
twist revealed: mychainlink.ca is registered at <strong>website.com</strong=
> (that's why it's "EXTERNAL" at Spaceship). She's filing a case with websi=
te.com =E2=80=94 the form shows Subject "Application locked", website addre=
ss mychainlink.ca, username KendalChain, password field (=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F=
 she's about to send her password =E2=80=94 I should flag not to include th=
e password; support never needs it; the form says optional for account refe=
rence but best practice: don't share passwords. Actually the form itself as=
ks for it optionally. I'll advise leaving password blank =E2=80=94 safer).<=
/div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The domain is "locked to the reg=
istrar" =E2=80=94 registrar lock (clientTransferProhibited status) is norma=
l; transferring a domain requires unlocking it and getting the transfer/EPP=
 code from website.com. So the whole situation: to move the domain to Space=
ship (or just fix DNS), she needs website.com's cooperation.</div><div clas=
s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Two paths with website.com:
A. Just fix DNS at website.com: point A record to Hyperlift's IP =E2=80=94 =
no transfer needed, faster. She'd need Hyperlift's target IP from Spaceship=
/Alf first.
B. Transfer the domain to Spaceship: unlock domain, get EPP/auth code, init=
iate transfer at Spaceship.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Her =
subject says "Application locked" =E2=80=94 she's asking about the lock. My=
 message should ask for: (1) how to remove registrar lock, (2) the authoriz=
ation/EPP code for transfer to Spaceship, OR alternatively (3) how to updat=
e DNS A records to point to her new host's IP (X.X.X.X) if she keeps regist=
ration there.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Write the message =
for the "Message*" box. Keep it clear and complete. Also tell her: leave th=
e Password field EMPTY (never email passwords; support doesn't need it =E2=
=80=94 their own note says optional).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Message draft:</div><hr><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hello,<=
/div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">I need help with my domain mycha=
inlink.ca (account username: KendalChain).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">My website is now hosted on Spaceship's Hyperlift platform, but =
the domain is registered with website.com and shows a registrar lock, so th=
e site cannot be connected properly =E2=80=94 browsers show a certificate e=
rror (ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID) when visiting mychainlink.ca.</div><div=
 class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Please help me with BOTH of these:</div><=
ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">UNLOCK the domain =
for transfer and provide my authorization/EPP code, so I can transfer mycha=
inlink.ca to Spaceship.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>In the meantime, I need to update the domain's DNS records to point to my =
new host. Please tell me how to change the A record for mychainlink.ca (and=
 <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.mychainlink.c=
a/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">www.mychainlink.ca</a>) in my acco=
unt, or make the change for me =E2=80=94 my host will give me the IP addres=
s to point to.</div></li></ol><h2>Thank you,
Kendal Symes
<a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"mailto:kendalsymes98@gmai=
l.com" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">kendalsymes98@gmail.com</a></h2=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Good. Also remind: password field bl=
ank. And note the EPP code will be sent to her registrar email =E2=80=94 ch=
eck spam. Keep short.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-ed=
ge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"s=
croll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></=
div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D""=
 class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v=
-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Mys=
tery SOLVED =E2=80=94 that's why everything's been fighting us: mychainlink=
.ca is registered at <strong>website.com</strong>, so Spaceship can't touch=
 its address book. The "lock" is the registrar lock, and only website.com c=
an lift it. You're exactly where you need to be with that support case =F0=
=9F=91=8F</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Two things before you =
send:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><stron=
g>Erase the Password field.</strong> Never send your password to support =
=E2=80=94 their own form says it's optional, and no legit rep needs it.</di=
v></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Paste this into the big <s=
trong>Message</strong> box:</div></li></ol><div data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v=
-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9=3D"" data-v-bfaa=
bce6=3D"" class=3D"sticky-release" style=3D"--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;=
