eight: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"=
><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container=
 toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div c=
lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She's asking about the video recorder icon =
being ugly =E2=80=94 presumably the camera capture button/icon in the app U=
I (the big circle shutter button in her screenshot? or a video recorder ico=
n somewhere). She wants to change it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Per memory rules:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">"never change her code's colors/styling without permission; she=
's the boss on all creative decisions" =E2=80=94 she IS asking for a change=
, so we can do it, but I should get her input on what she wants (creative d=
ecision is hers).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">This =
chat is read-only on the repo =E2=80=94 I can't push. Changes go through he=
r editing on GitHub (risky for a 4000-line file) or Kimi Claw (out of credi=
ts). OR I give her the code to paste.</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 which icon? In the screenshot: bottom toolba=
r had a circular refresh icon, a lightning bolt (flash), a big circle shutt=
er button, and a grid icon. The "video recorder icon" =E2=80=94 maybe on th=
e profile page there's a video icon, or the camera tab icon. She says "vide=
o recorder icon" =E2=80=94 likely the video camera icon used for "Go Live"/=
video chat, or the camera tab icon in the nav.</div><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">I need to find the icon in the code. The icon could be an em=
oji (=F0=9F=93=B9?) or an inline SVG. Let me search the file. I can't fetch=
 the whole 415KB file easily (truncation). GitHub code search API? The API =
search code requires auth. Hmm.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=
Options: fetch raw via jsdelivr and hope truncation includes it =E2=80=94 i=
t's a huge file; truncation shows the beginning. The icons are probably SVG=
 definitions near the top of the CSS or inline in HTML body. Could fetch <a=
 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh=
/mychainlinkCA/Mychainlink@main/index.html" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noop=
ener">https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/mychainlinkCA/Mychainlink@main/index.html=
</a> and search within returned text =E2=80=94 but truncation cut at ~5000 =
tokens earlier in the blob fetch. The icons might be within the first chunk=
 if defined early (SVG symbols often at top of body).</div><div class=3D"pa=
ragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also =E2=80=94 how would we change it? Read-only chat=
: she edits, or Claw (no credits). But maybe the icon is defined in an earl=
y part of the file I can locate and give her an exact small edit (find line=
, replace SVG snippet). That's feasible: give her the exact old snippet to =
Ctrl+F and the new snippet to paste.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto">First, identify the icon. Ask her which icon exactly? She said "video =
recorder icon" =E2=80=94 in the screenshot's bottom bar there's a shutter c=
ircle... Actually in the screenshot toolbar: refresh (flip camera), lightni=
ng (flash), big hollow circle (shutter), grid (gallery?). Hmm, "video recor=
der" =E2=80=94 maybe the camera tab icon in the bottom nav (Home, Explore, =
Camera, Messages, Profile)? That nav had icons: "MyChainLink ?" placeholder=
s in my fetch (SVGs didn't render as text).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">Rather than guess, ask one quick clarifying question with optio=
ns: (a) the big round shutter button on the camera screen, (b) the Camera t=
ab icon in the bottom menu, (c) the video-chat/live icon elsewhere. But bet=
ter: fetch the file head and look for video-camera SVG symbols, then show h=
er options.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me try fetching =
the file via jsdelivr to find icon definitions. Risk: truncated. Worth a tr=
y =E2=80=94 web_open_url.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also m=
emory: full code always, she's boss on styling. And one step at a time. Fir=
st step: locate the icon. Let me fetch.</div></div></div></div></div> <div =
class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></d=
iv><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></=
div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div =
data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div=
 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">We absolutely can =E2=80=94 you're the creative director, I'm just the =
hands. First I need to find the little guy in your code and see what we're =
working with (is it an emoji, a built-in icon, a custom drawing?). Let me d=
ig:</div></div></div><div data-v-afe3a0d2=3D"" data-v-f179e12b=3D"" class=
