kdown-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"m=
arkdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Statically failed too. I can=
't easily read the 415KB file remotely. Options:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><=
div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Ask HER to find it: on GitHub file pag=
e, use "Search within code" / Ctrl+F, search for likely terms ("video", "sv=
g"), screenshot the matches. Then I identify the icon and give her exact re=
placement.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Or ask her t=
o describe/point at the exact icon first (which screen it's on). She said "=
video recorder icon" =E2=80=94 looking at her screenshot: bottom toolbar of=
 the camera screen had: flip-camera icon, lightning bolt, big hollow circle=
 (shutter), grid. The "video recorder" =E2=80=94 hmm, maybe she means the s=
hutter button? Or maybe in the bottom nav, the "Camera" tab icon looks like=
 a video camera.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Simpl=
est division: ask her which screen it's on + get her to Ctrl+F on the GitHu=
b page. Actually, GitHub blob page has a "Search within code" box (visible =
in her earlier screenshots). She can search "video" and screenshot results.=
</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But wait =E2=80=94 better idea:=
 I can search GitHub code via web_search? GitHub code search isn't indexed =
well.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Alternative: I recall the =
app has emoji icons in places (=F0=9F=8E=B5, =F0=9F=94=92, =E2=AD=90, =F0=
=9F=93=B9?). The commit patches I read earlier included emoji usage (=F0=9F=
=94=92=E2=AD=90=F0=9F=93=B9=F0=9F=8E=B5 etc. in premium features list). The=
 video camera emoji =F0=9F=93=B9 is likely used as an icon somewhere ("Vide=
o Chat =E2=AD=90..." used =F0=9F=93=B9 in "=F0=9F=93=B9 Video Chat"). So th=
e "video recorder icon" may literally be the =F0=9F=93=B9 emoji somewhere o=
n screen =E2=80=94 e.g., in nav or camera UI.</div><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto">Given limited remote visibility, the efficient move: ask her =
to point at it precisely (which screen + where) AND/OR use GitHub's in-page=
 search. Let me give her ONE simple task: on the GitHub file page (<a data-=
v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://github.com/mychainlinkCA/=
Mychainlink/blob/main/index.html" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">http=
s://github.com/mychainlinkCA/Mychainlink/blob/main/index.html</a>), use the=
 "Search within code" box, type <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">=F0=9F=93=B9</code> (or "video"), scree=
nshot what highlights. Hmm, typing emoji on Chromebook is annoying.</div><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Better: ask first which screen the ugly=
 icon lives on =E2=80=94 bottom camera toolbar, bottom nav, or somewhere el=
se =E2=80=94 and describe it. One question, zero work for her. Then next st=
ep I give her search term.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actua=
lly =E2=80=94 even better: I could have her open the site, right-click the =
icon =E2=86=92 Inspect... too technical.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">One clarifying question with concrete options based on her screen=
shot. Keep it light.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edg=
e-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"sc=
roll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></d=
iv></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div></div></div></div> <div da=
ta-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail is-open"><div data-v-0a72=
2276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" clas=
s=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail-divider"></div> <!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"=
" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D=
"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Your file's a b=
it too chunky for me to peek inside from here (it's 4000+ lines =E2=80=94 t=
he elevator only goes partway up). No problem =E2=80=94 you can be my eyes.=
 One quick question:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Whi=
ch screen is the ugly icon on?</strong></div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=F0=9F=93=B7 The <strong>camera screen</strong>=
 =E2=80=94 the row of buttons under the live video (like in your screenshot=
: flip, lightning, the big circle, grid)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">=F0=9F=A7=AD The <strong>bottom menu bar</strong> (Home, =
Explore, Camera, Messages, Profile)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Somewhere else =E2=80=94 describe it or send me a screenshot w=
ith a finger pointing at the offender =F0=9F=91=89</div></li></ol><div clas=
s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The moment I know which one and what it looks =
like, I'll find it in the code and we'll design you a prettier one. You're =
the art director =E2=80=94 you pick the look, I make it happen =F0=9F=8E=A8=
</div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!---->=
