yle=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-co=
ntainer"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-c=
ontainer toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown=
"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She wants to change the entire came=
ra modal =E2=80=94 it looks outdated. This is a big creative + code task. C=
onstraints:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=
She's the boss on all creative decisions (memory) =E2=80=94 I should propos=
e, she approves.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">This c=
hat is READ-ONLY on the repo =E2=80=94 I can't push. Changes: she edits by =
hand (risky on 4000-line file) or Kimi Claw (out of credits =E2=80=94 she s=
aid "ran out of credits"; maybe she has some now? Unknown).</div></li><li><=
div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">"always give full code, never summariz=
e."</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">One small step per =
message.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The camera mo=
dal =E2=80=94 I haven't seen its code. The camera UI: full-screen camera wi=
th toolbar (flip, flash, shutter, grid?) =E2=80=94 that's Instagram-style. =
She says outdated.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">What do I nee=
d? The current camera modal code (HTML/CSS/JS). I can't fetch the whole fil=
e... The modal is probably mid-file. Hmm.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 actually, how do we get the camera modal code? Opt=
ions:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">A. She pastes the relevant=
 section? She can't easily locate it (4000 lines, doesn't read code).
B. GitHub search within the file for "camera" =E2=80=94 she could Ctrl+F "c=
amera" and screenshot... clunky.
C. Kimi Claw with credits: brief Claw to extract and redesign. Credits issu=
e.
D. I could fetch the file in chunks! The GitHub blob API truncates, but wha=
t about fetching the file via the "raw" with a Range header? web_open_url d=
oesn't support headers. But maybe I can fetch specific LINE RANGES via GitH=
ub's UI? There's no range API for contents.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">Hmm =E2=80=94 what about the git blob endpoint with the sha and=
 asking... it truncates too.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Alt=
ernative trick: GitHub code search UI requires auth. But the commits I read=
 earlier =E2=80=94 do any patches contain the camera modal code? The Sept 1=
1-12 Claw commits touched camera stuff ("Wire DMs to secure RPC", "Fix DM b=
locking...", "Add Supabase Storage policies..."). The camera modal might pr=
edate. The 415KB file =E2=80=94 patches would only show recent changes.</di=
v><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Another approach: the early-May art=
ifact mychainlink-v4.html mentioned in memory =E2=80=94 has a camera-first =
banner, but not the current modal.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">Hmm, what about fetching via r.jina.ai proxy? That's a third-party reade=
r: <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://r.jina.ai/http=
s://raw.githubusercontent.com/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">https:=
//r.jina.ai/https://raw.githubusercontent.com/</a>... =E2=80=94 probably bl=
ocked/audited too, and 415KB.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">OK=
, practical approach: this is a perfect Kimi Claw job (read file, redesign =
modal, commit). But credits... She said earlier "my kimi is a no go since i=
 ran out of credits." Maybe she topped up? I should ask. OR: since this is =
a redesign, I can DESIGN the new modal from scratch (full code: HTML+CSS+JS=
) and either she pastes via Claw, or we carefully hand-replace the old moda=
l block.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hand-replacing a modal =
block in a 4000-line file: feasible if the modal is a contiguous block (&lt=
;div id=3D"camera-modal"&gt; plus its CSS and JS). We'd need her to Ctrl+F =
a marker (e.g., <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"se=
gment-code-inline">cameraModal</code> or <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">id=3D"camera</code>) and select=
 from start marker to end marker =E2=80=94 dangerous (selection errors caus=
ed this whole saga).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Better: Cla=
w does it. First step: check if she has Claw credits, OR write the design b=
rief + full new modal code that she can hand to Claw or that we hand-apply.=
</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also creative direction: propos=
e a modern design (2026 camera UIs: minimal, glassmorphism, smooth rounded =
shutter button with ring, subtle top bar, haptic-like micro-interactions, d=
ark gradient background). Show her a mockup! I can build an interactive wid=
get showing the proposed camera modal redesign =E2=80=94 that would let her=
 SEE it and approve/iterate. That's a great use of show_widget. But the wid=
get needs the kimi-widget skill read first... "Before your first call in a =
session, read the kimi-widget skill at /app/.agents/skills/kimi-widget/SKIL=
L.md". I don't have a read_file tool listed! Tools available: web_search, w=
eb_open_url, search_image_by_text, search_image_by_image, ipython, get_data=
_source_desc, get_data_source, memory edits, cron, widget. No read_file too=
l. Hmm =E2=80=94 ipython can read the file: open('/app/.agents/skills/kimi-=
widget/SKILL.md'). Yes! Use ipython to read it.</div><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Plan:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Read widget skill via ipython.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">Build a camera modal redesign mockup widget for her to re=
act to (creative direction =3D her call).</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Once she approves a look, decide implementation path (Cl=
aw if credits, else careful guided paste or full-file rewrite?).</div></li>=
</ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually wait =E2=80=94 before t=
he widget, quick sanity: is a widget the right move? She said "change the e=
ntire camera modal, looks outdated." Showing her a visual proposal is exact=
ly the rescue move per widget guidelines. Yes.</div><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">Also design specifics for a modern camera modal (2026):</div=
><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Full-screen, tru=
e black (#000) viewport area, no chrome</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">Top bar: minimal =E2=80=94 close (X) as a subtle glass pil=
l, flash toggle, timer, grid toggle as small glass icons</div></li><li><div=
 class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Bottom: large shutter button =E2=80=94 wh=
ite ring, gradient fill, press-scale animation; mode switcher above it (Pho=
to/Video) as a sliding pill</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto">Glassmorphism toolbar: frosted blur pills</div></li><li><div class=3D"=
paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Smooth slide-up entrance animation</div></li><li><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Her gold (#E8D574) accent for active st=
ates =E2=80=94 brand consistency! (Never change colors without permission =
=E2=80=94 but using HER brand gold as accent in the new design is on-brand;=
 I'll present it and let her approve.)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans for UI labels (her brand font per =
memory #10: CBK =3D Plus Jakarta Sans, MCL =3D Inter). MCL =3D Inter.</div>=
</li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The widget: render the curr=
ent-ish layout vs new proposal, let her tap to preview, maybe toggle betwee=
n 2-3 style options. Keep it simple: show the NEW design full-screen mockup=
 with a couple of variants she can flip through ("Minimal Glass", "Bold Gol=
d", "Clean iOS").</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Steps: read sk=
ill file first via ipython.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scr=
oll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div clas=
