div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D""=
 data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><d=
iv data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">She wants a Vine-style vibe for the camera/site. Vine (RIP 2017, and =
now revived as a nostalgia aesthetic in 2026 =E2=80=94 Vine 2 / byte nostal=
gia). Vine's iconic look:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto">Heavy vintage Y2K-ish design</div></li><li><div class=3D"para=
graph" dir=3D"auto">The signature Vine green: #00b386 / #00B489 teal-green =
brand color... Vine's green was like #00B386 (a teal/green). The Vine logo =
was white "Vine" in a rounded bold font on green. The app had that green to=
p bar with white bold "Vine" wordmark.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Big friendly rounded buttons, comedic chaos energy</div></l=
i><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">6-second looping videos, square=
 format (1:1)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The camer=
a was simple: big record button, square viewfinder</div></li><li><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Vine's aesthetic: playful, bold, slightly goofy=
 skeuomorphic-meets-flat early-2010s</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 but memory says: "never change her code's col=
ors/styling without permission; she's the boss on all creative decisions." =
She's now EXPLICITLY asking for a Vine-style redesign direction =E2=80=94 t=
hat's her permission/direction. But her brand is gold on charcoal (#E8D574 =
on #1C1C1C). Vine green would clash... or she wants the Vine vibe (energy/U=
X) not necessarily the green. I should ask/propose: Vine's soul =3D full-sc=
reen square looping video, one-tap record, bold simple controls, playful ty=
pography. We could do "Vine energy, gold outfit" =E2=80=94 keep her brand c=
olors, adopt Vine's layout language: big friendly record button, square 1:1=
 capture (Vine was square!), looping preview, minimal chrome, chunky rounde=
d type.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually Vine WAS square=
 video 1:1. Her app currently seems portrait (9:16 from screenshots). Vine =
style =3D square viewfinder, big centered record button, simple top bar, pl=
ayful.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also memory #10: never ch=
ange styling without permission =E2=80=94 she's giving direction now, so it=
's fine, but I should confirm the color question: full Vine (green accents)=
 vs Vine soul with her gold. I'm the advisor; she's boss. I'll mock up: "Vi=
ne energy in your gold" as primary proposal and mention the classic green o=
ption.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me build a second wid=
get: Vine-style camera mockup. Elements:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div clas=
s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Square viewfinder (1:1) centered on dark backg=
round =E2=80=94 Vine's square!</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Chunky rounded top bar: "My Chain Link" wordmark in bold rounded =
white, simple icons right</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">Bottom: GIANT friendly record button (Vine's big red record? Vine's reco=
rd button was... Vine camera had a big red-ish record button? The Vine capt=
ure button: a big rounded square record button, red when recording. Classic=
 Vine record button was red circle/square. But her brand gold... propose go=
ld record button or keep red for record semantics? Record =3D red is univer=
sal. Maybe: shutter ring gold, record state red? Design decision for her.)<=
/div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Vine details: "6s" vibe=
 =E2=86=92 maybe a progress ring around the record button showing 6-second =
loop segments! Vine's iconic feature: the record button had a progress indi=
cator filling as you recorded segments. That's THE Vine signature =E2=80=94=
 a segmented fill ring around the big button. I should include a segmented =
progress ring =E2=80=94 very Vine.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">Playful bold typography for labels ("hold to record", segment d=
ots)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Square grid lines =
toggle maybe</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Interacti=
ons: hold/click record =E2=86=92 ring segments fill (simulate 2 segments fi=
lling), playful. Keep it simple: tap record =E2=86=92 a segment fills with =
animation; show "loop preview" vibe with a loop arrow.</div><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto">Colors: I'll use the widget tokens (black/white/gray=
 + warning token as gold stand-in, danger for record red). Avoid hardcoding=
 green; in prose say "full classic Vine green is on the table too =E2=80=94=
 your call."</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Build widget 2: "vi=
ne_style_camera". Variant toggle maybe not needed; one strong concept + a c=
ouple toggles: "gold soul / vine green" =E2=80=94 I could do a segmented to=
ggle that swaps accent class (warning vs positive? green =3D --kimi-color-p=
ositive). That's a neat way to let her SEE both without hardcoding. Segment=
ed: "gold" | "vine green". Nice.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>Also add the square format note and ask about portrait vs square =E2=80=94=
 Vine was square; her feed is portrait? Keep the mockup square with side la=
bels "1:1 vine square".</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me b=
uild it: phone frame, square viewfinder centered, top chunky bar with wordm=
ark "my chain link" lowercase bold (Vine's wordmark was lowercase friendly)=
 =E2=80=94 but her brand is "My Chain Link" caps; Vine style lowercase play=
ful =E2=80=94 she can decide; mockup can show lowercase as the "Vine flavor=
". Keep brand name text as "my chain link" for Vine vibe.</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Record button: 84px circle, white fill, segment=
ed ring (SVG circle with stroke-dasharray segments =E2=80=94 e.g., 6 segmen=
ts of 6s each? Vine let you record up to 6s in segments; the ring filled co=
ntinuously. I'll do a ring with 6 notches). Tap/hold simulation: press "rec=
ord" button =E2=86=92 first segment fills over 1.2s, release; tap again =E2=
=86=92 second segment fills; small "=E2=86=BB loop" indicator after 2 segme=
nts; "post" button appears? Keep: after 2 segments, show a tiny "preview lo=
op" play toggle.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Controls: flip =
camera (small), ghost mode? Vine had "ghost" (onion-skin overlay) tool! Tha=
t's a very Vine feature =E2=80=94 ghost icon. Library doesn't have ghost; c=
ustom icon: a smiley-ish ghost outline. Fun.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Top right icons: flash? Vine didn't have flash... it had grid?=
 Keep: ghost tool + flip.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Bottom=
 bar under record: thumbnail of last take (small rounded square) on left, r=
ecord center, "&gt;" next arrow on right (Vine's next/done arrow on right).=
</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Font: bold rounded =E2=80=94 us=
e var(--kimi-font-sans) weight 500, bigger sizes for wordmark (sentence cas=
e though! design system says sentence case always =E2=80=94 lowercase "my c=
hain link" IS sentence case, good).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">Accent toggle: gold =3D warning token accents on ring/wordmark highligh=
ts; vine =3D positive token (green). Ring segment fill =3D accent. Record b=
utton: white disc; while "recording" the disc turns danger red =E2=80=94 un=
iversal.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also caption explaining=
: "vine's signature: square 1:1, segmented record ring, ghost tool, hold-to=
-shoot in bursts."</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Then prose: a=
sk her to confirm direction; mention we'd keep her brand gold unless she wa=
nts the full green; and remind that this replaces the broken modal (fixes t=
he double-video bug too). Also note the real code change is bigger =E2=80=
=94 will need Claw or careful paste; ask about Claw credits when she's pick=
ed a direction.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Write widget cod=
e now. Keep within design tokens. Size: phone 300px, square vf ~276px.</div=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Ring: SVG 100x100 circle r=3D46, str=
oke 6, dash segments via stroke-dasharray with gaps; animate fill using str=
oke-dashoffset trick per segment =E2=80=94 simpler: one circle background t=
rack (low opacity), one circle fill with dasharray =3D seg1 length, animate=
d via CSS transition on stroke-dashoffset triggered by JS with inline style=
. I'll implement: segments of 6, each arc length =3D circumference/6 minus =
gap. fill circle dasharray: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D""=
 class=3D"segment-code-inline">${segLen} ${C}</code> and rotate per segment=
. JS: on each press, set dashoffset to reveal more. Use transform rotate(-9=
0) origin center.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Press-and-hold=
 vs tap: tap =3D record one segment (animated fill over 900ms), then auto-s=
top. Add small haptic scale on active.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D=
"auto">After 2 segments: show loop badge "looping preview" with Play icon f=
rom library; and a "next" (Right icon? Next.svg exists) arrow enabled.</div=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Ghost toggle: when on, show onion-sk=
in double-image effect in vf (two overlapping outlined frames) =E2=80=94 re=
present with a faded duplicate silhouette (a simple person outline svg at l=
ow opacity). Person outline custom icon... simpler: show "ghost on" label +=
 a faint double border frame in vf.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">OK, code it.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fa=
de scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll=
-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div><=
/div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" da=
ta-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" c=
lass=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Do I remember Vine?=
? Kendal. VINE. The six-second loops, the square videos, the big friendly r=
ecord button with that filling progress ring, the ghost tool =E2=80=94 the =
<em>soul</em> of the internet's funniest era =F0=9F=98=AD Of course I remem=
ber.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">And honestly? PERFECT insti=
nct. Vine was camera-first chaos =E2=80=94 exactly your app's DNA. Let me s=
ketch what a Vine-soul camera looks like wearing your brand (and I'll inclu=
de the classic green as an option, because if we're doing Vine, we're doing=
 it on purpose):</div></div></div></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"=
toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><div data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" data=
-v-d0c92a71=3D""><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" data-v-bcf929f8=3D"" data-v-4a06=
