f2=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-content"><div class=3D"scrol=
l-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div data-v-b9=
0066f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0;"><=
div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D""=
 data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><d=
iv data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">She says "We better not copy it too close" =E2=80=94 worried about co=
pying Vine's IP/trademark. Smart instinct, boss. Reassure: we're taking <em=
>inspiration</em> from the layout language (square video, segmented record =
ring, ghost tool, minimal chrome) =E2=80=94 not Vine's trademarks, logo, na=
me, green brand color, or assets. Vine (X Corp) owns the Vine name/logo/gre=
en. Our version: different name, her gold, original icons, original wordmar=
k. Layout concepts and interaction patterns aren't copyrightable; we're bui=
lding an original design with a nostalgic vibe. Also "vine green" toggle =
=E2=80=94 if worried, drop the green, keep gold.</div><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">So: confirm gold-only (drop the vine-green option), origin=
al everything, "inspired-by" not "copy." Then still need answers: square vs=
 tall, and Claw credits. She answered neither yet. Re-ask briefly.</div><di=
v class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Keep it short and warm, praise her legal=
 instincts.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade sc=
roll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge=
-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div></div>=
</div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"=
toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31=
c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Look at you=
, playing lawyer at 5:30am =E2=80=94 and you're absolutely right =F0=9F=98=
=84 The instincts are good: we take the <em>vibe</em>, not the branding.</d=
iv><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Here's the clean line, and we're s=
taying well behind it:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Ours:</strong> the square loop idea, a record =
ring that fills in segments, a ghost/onion-skin tool, chunky minimal button=
s =E2=80=94 layouts and interaction ideas, which nobody owns</div></li><li>=
<div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=E2=9D=8C <strong>Never:</strong> the=
 Vine name, its logo, its exact green, or any of its actual artwork =E2=80=
=94 your name, your gold, icons we draw ourselves</div></li></ul><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Think "vine-inspired," like how every camera ap=
p on earth borrowed the pull-to-refresh idea. Original skeleton, nostalgic =
soul. And we'll drop the green toggle entirely =E2=80=94 <strong>gold only<=
/strong>, so nobody can even squint at it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">So, final two calls, art director:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div=
 class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Square loops or keep it tall?</st=
rong></div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Do you ha=
ve Kimi Claw credits for the build, or do we park the blueprint until you d=
o?</strong></div></li></ol></div></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" cla=
ss=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-ro=
llup__tail-in"><!----></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!-=
