s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Test: fetch <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"=
_blank" href=3D"https://mychainlink.ca/logo-favicon.jpg" rel=3D"noreferrer =
nofollow noopener">https://mychainlink.ca/logo-favicon.jpg</a> =E2=80=94 do=
es it serve? server.js express.static serves it. Let me check. Also check w=
hat the browser tab shows =E2=80=94 maybe the issue is the <code data-v-bfa=
abce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">?v=3D3</code>=
 query param? That shouldn't matter.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto">Possible causes:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">The browser cached an old broken favicon (during the broken site =
days, the tab icon 404'd; browsers cache favicons aggressively).</div></li>=
<li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The actual served content-type of=
 .jpg as icon works fine.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">On her phone (iOS Safari), apple-touch-icon uses the same jpg.</div></li=
></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually =E2=80=94 I can verify=
 by fetching the favicon URL. Let me do that.</div><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto">Also she said "broken again" =E2=80=94 maybe it shows a gener=
ic globe icon in the tab. Most likely explanation: stale favicon cache from=
 when the site was broken/placeholder. Fix: hard refresh, or wait for cache=
; or bump ?v=3D4 to force re-fetch. Simple fix: change ?v=3D3 to ?v=3D4 in =
the HTML (one tiny edit) to bust caches.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Let me verify the file serves on the live site first.</div></div>=
