lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She wants the main logo from the landing pa=
ge =E2=80=94 logo-v4.png (the transparent gold chain wordmark, per memory #=
10: "MCL logo =3D logo-v4.png (transparent) from GitHub repo"). Not my draw=
n approximation.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Problem: ipytho=
n has no network, so I can't download logo-v4.png from GitHub into the sand=
box... Can I? "No network" stated. But wait =E2=80=94 maybe outbound networ=
k is actually blocked; earlier the skill read worked locally. Let me test q=
uickly whether ipython can fetch (e.g., urllib to raw.githubusercontent). I=
f blocked, alternative: the landing page's logo is displayed in my earlier =
fetch of mychainlink.ca =E2=80=94 the chain logo appeared in the reader out=
put as an image; the fetch tool CAN display images. Maybe web_open_url of l=
ogo-v4.png renders it visually but I still can't get its bytes into the san=
dbox.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Options if no network in i=
python:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Try =
anyway (urllib) =E2=80=94 maybe only pip is blocked, not HTTP. Worth one te=
st.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">If blocked: build t=
he OG image as HTML/CSS referencing... no.</div></li><li><div class=3D"para=
graph" dir=3D"auto">Give her instructions to make it herself: she could scr=
eenshot/crop? Or simpler =E2=80=94 use logo-v4.png DIRECTLY as the og:image=
! The OG image doesn't have to be 1200=C3=97630; platforms accept any size,=
 they crop to aspect. Using <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=
=3D"https://mychainlink.ca/logo-v4.png" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener=
">https://mychainlink.ca/logo-v4.png</a> directly as og:image is zero-work:=
 just add the meta tags. Transparent PNG on some platforms renders on white=
 or dark =E2=80=94 fine.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">Simplest path honoring her wish: og:image =3D <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" ta=
rget=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://mychainlink.ca/logo-v4.png" rel=3D"noreferr=
er nofollow noopener">https://mychainlink.ca/logo-v4.png</a> (her real main=
 logo). Then meta tags only. If she wants a fancy banner later, we do it wh=
en Claw credits return (or she uploads a photo).</div><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">Let me test network quickly in ipython; if it works, I can=
 composite logo-v4.png onto the banner properly (download via urllib, paste=
). One attempt.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fad=
