2-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.14208 52.10112l259.686=
4 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 52.30592 51.93728l285.6=
96-287.744z" fill=3D"currentColor"></path></svg></div></div> <div data-v-b9=
0066f2=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-content"><div class=3D"s=
croll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div data-=
v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"height: 0px; opacity: 0=
;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-tex=
t"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">Interesting =E2=80=94 this looks like she's pasting output from =
some code analysis tool (maybe Kimi's code analysis on the repo, or she ask=
ed another AI). It gives me actual line numbers and class names of her came=
ra code:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Lin=
es 650-696: getUserMedia() camera functionality</div></li><li><div class=3D=
"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Line 653: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb3=
1c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-v{width:100%;height:100%;object-=
fit:cover;transform:scaleX(-1)}</code> =E2=80=94 the video element CSS</div=
></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Line 661: <code data-v-bfaa=
bce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-canvas{di=
splay:none}</code></div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So =
the camera modal is around lines 650-696 =E2=80=94 that's the CSS block are=
a? Line 653 with <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"s=
egment-code-inline">.cam-v</code> CSS and line 661 <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D=
"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-canvas</code> CS=
S =E2=80=94 these are CSS class definitions, meaning lines ~650-696 contain=
 CSS classes for the camera (<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"=
" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-v</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" d=
ata-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-canvas</code>). Wait=
, the analysis says "camera functionality at lines 650-696" referencing get=
UserMedia =E2=80=94 but line 653 shows a CSS rule. Maybe the file has CSS u=
p front (in the &lt;style&gt;&lt;style&gt;</div><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">Hmm, but 415KB file with style starting ~line 20... CSS could ea=
sily run to line 650+. Then HTML body and JS later (JS around 2618+ per ear=
lier patch context: the Terms gate was ~3496 in patch context... actually t=
he acceptTos patch showed lines around 2618 for TERMS_VERSION and 3496 for =
the terms check).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So this info i=
s partial. She needs to send me more =E2=80=94 I asked for the camera block=
 copy. This is her starting to deliver the map. The meta timestamp is 20:46=
 +08:00 (=3D 05:46 PDT) =E2=80=94 she's still at it.</div><div class=3D"par=
agraph" dir=3D"auto">My response: great, this confirms the camera pieces ex=
ist around line 650-696 (CSS) =E2=80=94 the JS getUserMedia is there too. T=
o build the replacement I need the actual code text. Next step: have her co=
py the block and paste it here.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=
How to guide her: open index.html in the GitHub editor (edit mode), Ctrl+F =
for <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-i=
nline">.cam-v</code> =E2=80=94 wait, in the editor, search "cam-v". Then se=
lect from around there... Actually better: since the camera CSS is lines ~6=
45-700 and modal HTML/JS elsewhere, the camera modal might be scattered (CS=
S in head, HTML modal in body, JS functions later). The double-video bug su=
ggests the video element + modal positioning issues.</div><div class=3D"par=
agraph" dir=3D"auto">Simplest ask: "Select lines 640 to 700 in the editor a=
nd copy-paste to me" =E2=80=94 GitHub web editor shows line numbers; she ca=
n click line 640, shift-click line 700, Ctrl+C, paste here. That's precise =
and safe (read-only copy).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But i=
s the whole camera story in 640-700? getUserMedia JS "referenced in camera =
functionality at lines 650-696" =E2=80=94 but line 653 shows CSS <code data=
-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-v<=
/code>... a JS function wouldn't be at 653 if 653 is CSS. The analysis summ=
ary may be sloppy. The CSS block <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-canvas{display:none}</code> at 661=
 and <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-=
inline">.cam-v</code> at 653 =E2=80=94 that's definitely CSS. So lines 650-=
696 are CSS for the camera UI. The JS (getUserMedia) is probably elsewhere,=
 maybe ~1000-1100 or later.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Plan=
: ask her to copy lines 640-710 (CSS) first =E2=80=94 paste to me. Then sep=
arately find the modal HTML &amp; JS. Actually let me first get her to past=
e 640-710. One step.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also acknow=
ledge the upload status? She didn't confirm og-image upload =E2=80=94 skip,=
 stay on camera. Actually she may have done it; I'll check later. Keep focu=
sed.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-ed=
ge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-m=
easure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div></div></div><=
/div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcal=
l-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" dat=
a-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" cl=
ass=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Ooh, now we're getti=
ng somewhere =E2=80=94 a code X-ray! =F0=9F=A9=BB This tells me your camera=
's pieces: the video feed element (<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb3=
1c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-v</code>), the hidden capture ca=
nvas (<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code=
-inline">.cam-canvas</code>), and the getUserMedia brain =E2=80=94 and that=
 the camera's <strong>styles</strong> live around lines 650=E2=80=93696. Th=
at's the map's first grid square.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
">I need to actually <em>read</em> those lines to build your replacement pr=
operly. Easy copy job, no editing:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Open =F0=9F=91=89 <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" targe=
t=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://github.com/mychainlinkCA/Mychainlink/edit/main=
/index.html" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener">https://github.com/mychai=
nlinkCA/Mychainlink/edit/main/index.html</a></div><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">In the editor, <strong>click on line 640</strong> (click right=
 on the line number), then <strong>scroll down, hold Shift, and click line =
710</strong>. That highlights the whole block. Press <strong>Ctrl+C</strong=
>, then paste it right here in our chat.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">That chunk is the camera's wardrobe (all its styling). Once I see=
 it, I'll tell you which other block to copy next =E2=80=94 the modal's ske=
leton and its brain come after =F0=9F=91=95=F0=9F=94=8D</div></div></div></=
div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail"><div data-v-=
