 (25/turn), be efficient. Actually =E2=80=94 maybe better to deliver in sta=
ges: first turn, do the build offline and deliver. Let me go.</div><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait, also the paste truncation: it ended at =
<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inlin=
e">document.addEvent&lt;/document&gt;</code> weird artifact =E2=80=94 the f=
ile content she uploaded is partial (ends mid-messages section). Fine =E2=
=80=94 I don't need beyond camera. But note her paste was huge =E2=80=94 I =
have plenty.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Design decisions fo=
r the new modal (her spec):</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Full-screen, theme-aware: use CSS vars. Dark: bg near-black=
; Light: bg near-white with dark text. Her theme vars: --bg, --surf, --ink,=
 --ink-2, --gold, --gold-hi, --gold-deep, --gold-edge, --gold-wash, --line,=
 --r, --r-pill, --r-lg, --ease, --ease-out, --font-b, --font-d, --sh-2/3, -=
-red, --green. I saw these used. For the camera overlay, using --bg-based s=
urface works for both themes. Video area stays raw feed (unstyled bg).</div=
></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Top bar: close (X) left? Cu=
rrent has X top-right. Widget 1 had close left + tools right. Keep X top-ri=
ght (matches her muscle memory)? Spec said "like the first example" which h=
ad close top-left... minor. I'll do close top-right to match existing behav=
ior (less confusion), tools row top-left? Hmm, widget 1: close left, flash/=
timer/grid right. Simplest: keep close top-right (existing), add mode pill =
at top center or above shutter.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Layout: bottom dock: mode pill (Photo | Video) above controls row=
 [switch | shutter | flash]; video mode shutter becomes record with 4-segme=
nt ring; recording auto-stops at 4s; tap again before 4s to stop early. Gri=
d button? Current has no grid (the "grid" icon in her screenshot was actual=
ly the cam-video button with film/grid SVG =E2=80=94 yes! <code data-v-bfaa=
bce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-video</co=
de> button has a grid/film icon SVG). So current buttons: switch, flash(=E2=
=9A=A1emoji), shutter, video(film icon). New design: mode pill replaces the=
 video button; keep flash + switch.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Multi-photo: keep in Photo mode (strip + counter 0/5, Retake/A=
dd/Done).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">After capture=
: existing preview panel with caption/font/color/location/Post/Retake + pre=
mium actions (Add to Story, Go Live) =E2=80=94 keep ALL of that functionali=
ty; restyle lightly to theme vars. Actually the preview panel CSS <code dat=
a-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-p=
review</code> etc. also gets replaced =E2=80=94 keep IDs and structure comp=
atible with finishCapture/postCam/retake.</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">DM mode: when _dmMode set (sendMediaMsg elsewhere), post=
Cam handles sending; the flow: capture =E2=86=92 preview =E2=86=92 Post (bu=
tton text changed by sendMediaMsg presumably). Must keep <code data-v-bfaab=
ce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-cap-action=
s</code> Post button class hook. I'll keep id-based hooks instead: give the=
 Post button id=3D"cam-post-btn"? But sendMediaMsg (code I haven't seen) ma=
y reference existing structure. Safer: keep the same class names &amp; stru=
cture in the preview panel (cam-cap-row, cam-cap-textarea, cam-cap-tools, c=
am-cap-actions) so unseen code keeps working. Only restyle visuals via CSS.=
</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">JS rewrite details:</=
div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Keep global v=
ars: camStream, camFacing('environment'), camPhotos, camData, camIsVideo, c=
amRecorder, camRecording, camVideoChunks.</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">openCam(): same guards; reset UI to photo mode default.<=
/div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">setCamMode('photo'|'vid=
eo'): pill slider, shutter appearance.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">snap(): unchanged core (draw, push, strip, flash effect).</=
div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">toggleVideo() =E2=86=92 =
replaced by startStopVideo() bound to shutter in video mode; 4s timer with =
ring; auto-stop. Also update <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"=
" class=3D"segment-code-inline">$('cam-video-btn')</code> references in clo=
seCam (classList remove 'on') =E2=80=94 since that element won't exist anym=
ore, must guard. closeCam references <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048c=
b31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">$('cam-flash-btn').classList.remove=
('on');$('cam-video-btn').classList.remove('on')</code> =E2=80=94 if I rewr=
ite closeCam too, fine (I'm rewriting the whole block). But OTHER code outs=
ide the block may reference cam-video-btn? grep: toggleVideo def, closeCam =
def =E2=80=94 both in block. OK.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Ring UI: SVG circle around shutter, 4 segments; progress via stro=
ke-dashoffset animation driven by JS timer (requestAnimationFrame or CSS tr=
ansition 4s linear).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Li=
ght mode: pill buttons use color-mix on --ink; on light theme --ink is dark=
 =E2=86=92 buttons dark-tinted on light bg. The video feed area: keep black=
 background behind video (camera letterboxing) =E2=80=94 fine in both theme=
s; chrome adapts.</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Alri=
ght =E2=80=94 also the stories: "Same loops set up for stories" =E2=80=94 s=
tories use the same camera capture then addToStory() (existing). Since cap =
lives in the camera video mode, stories get it automatically.</div><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me now write the build script. Steps:</di=
v><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Download index.=
html.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Extract the three=
 current blocks; save them as backup files too (so she can revert =E2=80=94=
 though GitHub history also works).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Compose new blocks.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Validate new JS with node --check (write JS to file, node --check=
).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Write 3 deliverable =
files: cam-css.txt, cam-html.txt, cam-js.txt with clear MARKERS as first/la=
st lines to help her paste (e.g., first line comment). Actually including m=
arker comments inside code helps her: CSS block starts with <code data-v-bf=
aabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D=
 CAMERA v2 =3D=3D=3D */</code> and ends right before <code data-v-bfaabce6=
=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFI=
LE =3D=3D=3D</code>.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">F=
or her paste instructions, each file's content is exactly what should repla=
ce the old region. I'll include the boundary comments in the files.</div><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Then the response: instructions per blo=
ck with exact search anchors:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">CSS: search <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D=
"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> (first match), =
select from there to just before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFILE</code> =E2=80=94 r=
eplace with file content.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">HTML: search <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"se=
gment-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code> select through the =
line before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segmen=
t-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 replace.</div></li>=
<li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">JS: search <code data-v-bfaabce6=
=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D CAMERA =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</code> select through the line befo=
re <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-in=
line">var editingPostId=3Dnull;</code> =E2=80=94 replace.
Then commit + Build in Hyperlift.</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">Careful with selection instructions: she'll click line of start=
 marker, shift-click end line. Workable.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">One concern: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" clas=
s=3D"segment-code-inline">postCam</code> in DM mode references <code data-v=
-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">document.=
querySelector('#cam-cap-actions .btn-primary')</code> =E2=80=94 but HTML us=
es class=3D"cam-cap-actions" (no id). So that query returns null =E2=86=92 =
guarded. In new HTML I'll add id=3D"cam-cap-actions" so it actually works (=
fixes latent bug). Harmless improvement.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Also <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"seg=
ment-code-inline">closeCam()</code> sets <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">$('cam-c').style.display=3D'fle=
x'</code> =E2=80=94 cam-c exists in new HTML. Keep id.</div><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D""=
 class=3D"segment-code-inline">updatePhotoStrip</code> manipulates <code da=
ta-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">$('ca=
m-cap-mode').querySelectorAll('button')[1]</code> =E2=80=94 keep those butt=
ons &amp; order in new HTML (Retake, Add, Done).</div><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">Let me write the new code now. I'll write the three new bl=
ocks in Python strings (careful with braces =E2=80=94 no f-strings; use pla=
in strings).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">New CSS (theme-awar=
