6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.counter</code> =
=E2=80=94 but updatePhotoStrip queries <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-04=
8cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">strip.querySelectorAll('.thumb')<=
/code> and inserts imgs before counter. Current CSS has no .cam-photo-strip=
 styling in the chunk? I saw <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"=
" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip</code> only in HTML; CSS f=
or it might be missing (maybe styled elsewhere or unstyled =E2=80=94 possib=
ly part of the "outdated" look). I'll style it.</div><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Note: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">$('cam-strip').classList.add('on')</code> =E2=80=
=94 display toggling via .on class. So: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-0=
48cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip{display:none}</=
code> <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code=
-inline">.cam-photo-strip.on{display:flex}</code>.</div><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">.cam-capture-actions: currently no CSS in chunk either! =
<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inlin=
e">.cam-capture-actions</code> gets class 'on' toggled; needs base display =
none + .on flex. More missing styles =E2=80=94 explains the janky look. I'l=
l style it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Preview panel: <code=
 data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.c=
