ode-inline">node --check /tmp/cam.js</code> via subprocess. Node may not be=
 installed... check. If not, do a basic sanity via esprima? Not available. =
Try node first.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">One more design =
consideration =E2=80=94 her instructions said gold shutter ring; light-mode=
: gold (#E8D574 family) works on light bg too. Buttons: color-mix ink tints=
 adapt. Video area stays black-bordered (the feed itself). The cam-wrap bg =
var(--bg) =E2=80=94 dark #0F0F0F-ish / light theme white. The video is abso=
lute inset 0 covering everything; chrome floats above. When video loads it'=
s full-bleed; bg only shows during load. Good.</div><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">Ring: r=3D46, C=3D2=CF=8046=E2=89=88289. dasharray set in JS=
.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also add small "REC" indicator=
? The shutter inner turns red square while recording (CSS .cam-wrap.vid .ca=
m-snap .inner is red square already in video mode... wait: inner becomes re=
d rounded square in VIDEO MODE always =E2=80=94 that reads as "record butto=
n" even when idle. Better: idle video mode: inner white circle smaller? Hmm=
. Design: photo mode: white disc; video idle: white disc with red dot cente=
r? recording: red square + ring fills. Let me do: video mode idle inner =3D=
 white disc with small red dot (via box-shadow inset?). Simpler: video idle=
: white ring disc (border red?)... Keep simple: video idle inner =3D white =
disc; add .recording state: inner becomes red square. Video mode signaled b=
y pill + red-tinted shutter border: .cam-wrap.vid .cam-snap{border-color:va=
r(--red)}. Recording: inner =E2=86=92 red square (CSS transition), ring gol=
d fills. Good.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Write it all now.=
 Also remember: keep <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
