-container toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdo=
wn"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She's on her phone in the GitHub =
editor, scrolled near lines 613-650. The screenshots show code BEFORE the <=
code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline=
">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA =3D=3D=3D</code> marker:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><di=
v class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Screenshot 1 (lines 623-634): <code data=
-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=
=3D=3D POST GALLERY (multi-photo) =3D=3D=3D */</code> =E2=80=94 <code data-=
v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.post-ga=
llery</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segm=
ent-code-inline">.post-gallery-inner</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" dat=
a-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.post-gallery-item</code>, =
<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inlin=
e">.post-gallery-dots</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D=
"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.post-gallery-dot.active</code> =E2=80=94 =
this is the FEED's multi-photo gallery carousel (displaying posts with mult=
iple photos in the feed). NOT the camera.</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Screenshot 2 (lines 629-639): continuation =E2=80=94 <co=
de data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">=
.post-gallery-count</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D""=
 class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cmt-sect</code> comments section styles.</d=
iv></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Screenshot 3 (lines 613-6=
22): <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-=
inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PHOTO STRIP (camera multi-photo) =3D=3D=3D */</code> =
=E2=80=94 <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-=
code-inline">.cam-photo-strip</code> (bottom:90px, rgba(0,0,0,.55), blur), =
<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inlin=
e">.cam-photo-strip .thumb</code> (52px), <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v=
-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip .counter</cod=
e>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-i=
nline">.cam-capture-actions</code> (bottom:42px) =E2=80=94 WAIT. This IS ca=
mera-related CSS, but it sits BEFORE the CAMERA marker! There are camera st=
yles outside my replacement boundary!</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">Screenshot 4 (lines 637-651): comments CSS ending, then line=
 650: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code=
-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA =3D=3D=3D</code> marker, line 651: <code data-=
v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-wra=
p{position:fixed;inset:0;background:#0B0B0A;...</code>.</div></li><li><div =
class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Screenshot 5: same as 1 (duplicate).</div>=
</li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So the structure differs fr=
om what I computed! My download-based extraction showed <code data-v-bfaabc=
e6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAM=
ERA</code> followed by <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" clas=
s=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-wrap{position:fixed;inset:0;background:#0B0B=
0A...</code>. And separately there was <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-04=
8cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PHOTO STRIP (camera =
multi-photo) =3D=3D=3D */</code> with <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048=
cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip</code> styles BEF=
ORE the camera marker (my NEW_CSS redefines .cam-photo-strip, .cam-capture-=
actions too).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 in =
my original file analysis, the camera CSS block I extracted (from <code dat=
a-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=
=3D=3D CAMERA</code> to <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" cla=
ss=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFILE</code>) did NOT include .ca=
m-photo-strip styles =E2=80=94 those are in the "PHOTO STRIP" section befor=
e the CAMERA marker. And the paste she sent earlier showed <code data-v-bfa=
abce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-st=
rip</code> in HTML but the CSS chunk she pasted (from my request lines 640-=
710) included... hmm, her paste started at the tail of comments CSS and inc=
luded <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code=
-inline">.cam-photo-strip</code>? Let me recall her earlier paste: it began=
 with <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code=
-inline">.cmt-react span</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cmt-row input</code>, then <code data-=
v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=
=3D=3D CAMERA =3D=3D=3D</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-wrap</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=
=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-v</code>, <co=
de data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">=
.cam-canvas</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-c</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-0=
48cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-snap</code>, <code data-v-b=
faabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-switch=
</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-c=
ode-inline">.cam-x</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" =
class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-flash</code>, <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D""=
 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-video</code>, <cod=
e data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.=
cam-preview</code>... I don't remember <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-04=
8cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip</code> in the pa=
ste =E2=80=94 the old camera block apparently did NOT contain .cam-photo-st=
rip/.cam-capture-actions CSS (that's why they looked unstyled! The "PHOTO S=
TRIP" section at 615-622 DID style them though... wait it does: <code data-=
v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-pho=
to-strip{...bottom:90px;background:rgba(0,0,0,.55);backdrop-filter:blur(8px=
)...}</code> =E2=80=94 so they WERE styled, in a separate section).</div><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So the file has camera styles in TWO pl=
aces:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><code =
data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =
=3D=3D=3D PHOTO STRIP (camera multi-photo) =3D=3D=3D */</code> (lines ~615-=
622): .cam-photo-strip + .cam-capture-actions</div></li><li><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" clas=
s=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA =3D=3D=3D */</code> (line 650=
+): .cam-wrap, .cam-v, etc.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">My NEW_CSS (file 1) redefines .cam-photo-strip and .cam-capture-actio=
ns with v2 styles (different positions: bottom:150px etc.). If the OLD PHOT=
O STRIP section remains, there will be DUPLICATE/conflicting rules =E2=80=
=94 CSS later rules win at equal specificity; the old section (line 615) co=
mes BEFORE the camera section (650)... where did she paste file 1? She repl=
aced from <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-=
code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> to before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"=
" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFILE</=
code> =E2=80=94 so my new CSS is at ~line 650+. The old PHOTO STRIP section=
 at 615 remains, and since 615 &lt; 650, my new rules override the old ones=
 for the same selectors (equal specificity =E2=86=92 later wins). So .cam-p=
hoto-strip: old says bottom:90px, new says bottom:150px =E2=86=92 new wins.=
</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So it's SAFE to leave it =E2=80=
=94 my v2 rules override because they come later in the file. No need for h=
er to delete anything (deleting adds risk). The leftover is dead weight but=
 harmless.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 is the=
re anything in the old PHOTO STRIP section that my new CSS does NOT redefin=
e and that would look wrong? The old section has:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li>=
<div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048=
cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip</code> =E2=9C=93 =
redefined</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><code data-v-=
bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo=
-strip.on</code> =E2=9C=93 redefined</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segm=
ent-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip .thumb</code> =E2=9C=93 redefined (44px v=
s old 52px =E2=80=94 fine)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-i=
nline">.cam-photo-strip .thumb:hover, .active</code> =E2=9C=93 redefined</d=
iv></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"=
" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-photo-strip .coun=
ter</code> =E2=9C=93 redefined</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-=
code-inline">.cam-capture-actions</code> =E2=9C=93 redefined</div></li><li>=
<div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048=
cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cam-capture-actions.on</code> =E2=
=9C=93 redefined</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">All c=
overed. Good =E2=80=94 the old rules lose to the new ones. Nothing to remov=
e.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also the POST GALLERY section=
 (625-634): that's the feed carousel =E2=80=94 completely separate feature,=
 leave it 100% alone.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">And <code =
data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.cm=
t-*</code> comments styles =E2=80=94 leave alone.</div><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">So my answer:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"para=
graph" dir=3D"auto">The POST GALLERY + comments stuff =E2=80=94 not camera,=
 leave it, hands off.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">T=
he PHOTO STRIP section =E2=80=94 it IS old camera styling, but you don't ne=
ed to remove it: my new file re-declares all of it and comes later in the f=
ile, so the new gold styles win automatically. Leaving it is the safe move =
(less surgery). Optional cleanup later.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">She's pasted file 1 already =E2=80=94 did she commit? She =
said "I pasted the first file" =E2=80=94 unclear if committed. Next: file 2=
 (HTML) and file 3 (JS). Remind: don't test between HTML/JS swaps; commit e=
ach; Build at the end.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>One question =E2=80=94 did her paste go in the right place? She said she p=
asted the first file; I'll trust and verify at Build time. Keep answer shor=
t: leave everything before the marker untouched.</div></div></div></div></d=
iv> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"=
true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D=
"true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></di=
v><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup_=
_flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"mark=
down-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"=
paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Great eyes, boss =E2=80=94 and great question. I ch=
ecked every screenshot against my build notes. Here's the verdict:</div><di=
v class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>=F0=9F=93=A6 Lines 625=E2=80=936=
48 (POST GALLERY + comments) =E2=80=94 hands off.</strong> That's your <em>=
feed's</em> multi-photo carousel and comment styles. Different feature, not=
 the camera. Zero touching.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><str=
ong>=F0=9F=93=B7 Lines 615=E2=80=93622 (PHOTO STRIP) =E2=80=94 old camera s=
tyles, but LEAVE THEM.</strong> You're right that it's camera stuff before =
the marker =E2=80=94 it's the old photo-strip/capture-button styling. Here'=
s the beautiful part: <strong>you don't need to delete it.</strong> My new =
CSS re-declares every one of those pieces, and since it sits <em>later</em>=
 in the file, the new gold styles automatically win the tug-of-war. The old=
 block becomes harmless dead weight =E2=80=94 no surgery needed, less risk.=
 We can sweep it out another day when Kimi Claw has hands again.</div><div =
class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So: <strong>change nothing above the <code=
 data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/*=
 =3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> marker.</strong> Just make sure file 1's paste sta=
rts exactly at the marker line and the old camera CSS below it got replaced=
.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">When that's committed, we move=
 to <strong>file 2 (the HTML skeleton)</strong> =E2=80=94 same dance: searc=
h <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inl=
ine">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code>, highlight to just before <code d=
ata-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;=
!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code>, replace with file 2's contents. Tell me when fi=
le 1 is committed and you're ready for file 2 =F0=9F=8E=AC=F0=9F=92=9B</div=
></div></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tai=
l"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></di=
