dentify which app froze GitHub editor or mychainlink.ca</span></div> <!----=
> <div data-v-064cc47f=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-title-container-extra"> <svg =
data-v-064cc47f=3D"" xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink=3D"ht=
tp://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden=3D"true" role=3D"img" class=3D"icon=
ify toolcall-title-container-extra-arrow" width=3D"1em" height=3D"1em" view=
Box=3D"0 0 1024 1024" name=3D"Right_b"><path d=3D"M681.00096 549.23264a36.8=
64 36.864 0 0 0-0.08192-52.0192L395.22304 211.47648a36.864 36.864 0 1 0-52.=
14208 52.10112l259.6864 259.72736-259.76832 261.69344a36.864 36.864 0 0 0 5=
2.30592 51.93728l285.696-287.744z" fill=3D"currentColor"></path></svg></div=
></div> <div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-co=
ntent"><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"=
true"></div><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"h=
eight: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"=
><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container=
 toolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div c=
lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">"The app just froze up on me" =E2=80=94 rig=
ht after the camera edits? Timeline: 07:05 she was asking about the code be=
fore CAMERA; 07:15 "Great the app just froze up on me."</div><div class=3D"=
paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 did she commit and Build already? If=
 the camera v2 went live and the app froze... or the GitHub editor froze (b=
ig file on mobile editor can freeze). "The app" =E2=80=94 could mean:</div>=
<ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The GitHub editor=
 app on her phone froze (plausible =E2=80=94 415KB file in mobile web edito=
r)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">My Chain Link the si=
te froze</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The whole phon=
e</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Most likely: GitHub'=
s mobile editor froze while doing the pastes (the editor struggles with hug=
e files on phones). This was the risk of phone editing.</div><div class=3D"=
paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Response: stay calm, ask which app froze + one fix:=
 don't force-quit mid-edit... actually if GitHub editor froze, the edits mi=
ght not be saved. Steps: wait a few seconds; if frozen, close the tab, reop=
en the edit link fresh =E2=80=94 check whether the pastes are still there (=
GitHub drafts? The web editor does NOT autosave reliably; a reload loses un=
committed edits!). That's the risk.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">If the site froze after Build =E2=80=94 different story: camera v2 migh=
t have a runtime bug. But she probably hasn't committed/Built yet (10 minut=
es elapsed since "can I commit all at once"). So most likely the editor fro=
ze.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Keep response short, one que=
stion: which app froze =E2=80=94 the GitHub editing page or the mychainlink=
.ca site? And immediate tip: leave the frozen page alone for a minute (it m=
ay catch up), don't mash buttons.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
">Also practical: the GitHub mobile app vs browser. She was in Safari on iP=
hone editing a 4000-line file =E2=80=94 freezing is expected honestly.</div=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also =E2=80=94 if edits lost, not a =
disaster: files are saved in chat; she re-pastes. Reassure.</div></div></di=
v></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria=
-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" ari=
a-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> =
<!----></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolc=
all-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" cl=
ass=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><di=
v class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Breathe =E2=80=94 which app froze, boss?=
</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=F0=9F=93=
=B1 <strong>The GitHub editing page?</strong> (Most likely =E2=80=94 that f=
ile is 4,000+ lines and phones hate chewing it.) If so: don't mash anything=
, give it 60 seconds to catch its breath. If it's truly stuck, close the ta=
b =E2=80=94 worst case the uncommitted pastes vanish, and that's <em>fine</=
em>, the three files are safe in our chat and we re-paste. Nothing is lost =
but minutes.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=F0=9F=8C=
=90 <strong>Your actual site (mychainlink.ca)?</strong> Only possible if yo=
u already committed AND hit Build =E2=80=94 did you?</div></li></ul><div cl=
ass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Either way, nothing's on fire. Files are saf=
e, the plan is safe, and the undo button exists on the other side. Tell me =
which one froze and we take the next step =F0=9F=A7=8A=F0=9F=96=A4</div></d=
iv></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail"><=
