/div> <div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-cont=
ent"><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-top" aria-hidden=3D"tr=
ue"></div><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"hei=
ght: 0px; opacity: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><=
div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container t=
oolcall-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The screenshots show the Chromebook editor wi=
th file 1 (CSS) already pasted: line 651 shows <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" d=
ata-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA v2 =
=E2=80=94 gold ring shutter, Photo/Video modes, 4s loops =3D=3D=3D */</code=
> and the new CSS runs through line ~698, ending right before <code data-v-=
bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=
=3D PROFILE</code> at line 699. The paste landed PERFECTLY =E2=80=94 old ca=
mera CSS is replaced, new v2 CSS in place, PROFILE section intact right aft=
er.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The "Commit changes..." butt=
on is green and ready. Since she said "I can commit all at the same time" a=
nd her plan was one commit =E2=80=94 she still needs to do file 2 (HTML) an=
d file 3 (JS) before committing. But wait =E2=80=94 the phone attempt may h=
ave already pasted some/all? On the phone it froze and the tab died; uncomm=
itted edits lost. Now on Chromebook, she pasted file 1 again (visible). Has=
 she done files 2 and 3? The screenshots only show the CSS region.</div><di=
v class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Tell her: file 1 is PERFECT =E2=80=94 co=
nfirm landmarks (CAMERA v2 header at 651, ends right before PROFILE at 699)=
. Now file 2 and file 3 before committing. Guide: for file 2, Ctrl+F <code =
data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt=
;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code>... in the GitHub editor, Ctrl+F works. Th=
en select to just before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" cl=
ass=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code>, paste file 2. T=
hen file 3: search <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D=
"segment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code>... but careful =E2=80=94 after pasting file 3? N=
o wait, order: HTML first, then JS. For JS search term: <code data-v-bfaabc=
e6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostI=
d=3Dnull;</code> is the END anchor; start anchor <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D""=
 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D CAMERA =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</code>.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Important editor tip: after pasting file 1, the editor may scr=
oll. Use Ctrl+F for each anchor. GitHub editor find: Ctrl+F opens search bo=
x.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Give next step: file 2 paste.=
 One instruction. Also warn: don't click Commit yet =E2=80=94 wait until al=
l three are in.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fad=
e scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-=
edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div></=
div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=
=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb3=
1c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb=
31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">BOSS. Loo=
k at that =E2=80=94 <strong>file 1 landed perfectly</strong> =F0=9F=91=8F L=
ine 651 opens with <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D=
"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA v2 =E2=80=94 gold ring shutter...=
</code>, and it closes exactly one line before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" d=
ata-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFILE</cod=
e> at 699. Clean borders, old wardrobe gone, new gold wardrobe in place. Th=
at's a textbook paste.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Now =E2=
=80=94 <strong>don't click Commit yet</strong> (I know that green button is=
 calling your name =F0=9F=98=84). Files 2 and 3 first, then one commit.</di=
v><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Next: the skeleton (file 2)=
.</strong> In the editor:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto">Press <strong>Ctrl+F</strong>, type <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"=
" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY=
 --&gt;</code>, press Enter (it jumps you there =E2=80=94 far below, in the=
 HTML body)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Click at th=
e start of that line, then Shift-click at the very start of the line that s=
ays <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-i=
nline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> (that selects everything from the cam=
era overlay down to just before Lightbox)</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Press <strong>Delete</strong>, then paste <strong>everyt=
hing from file 2</strong></div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">One caution: the <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code> text might ap=
pear twice after your search (the comment could show in the find box AND in=
 code) =E2=80=94 you're clicking the line <strong>in the code</strong>, not=
 in the search popup.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Tell me wh=
en file 2 is in and I'll spot-check before you do file 3 =F0=9F=A6=B4=F0=9F=
=94=8D</div></div></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-=
rollup__tail"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail-in">=
