 data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content-text"><d=
iv data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Looking at the screenshots: I see a problem forming!</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Line 2295: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-04=
8cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;/div&gt;</code> (end of previ=
ous section)
Line 2296: (blank)
Line 2297: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment=
-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 OLD one
Line 2298: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment=
-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 DUPLICATE! Her=
 new paste starts here
Line 2299: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment=
-code-inline">&lt;div class=3D"cam-wrap" id=3D"cam-o"&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 =
NEW v2 HTML</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 it lo=
oks like there's a duplicate <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"=
" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code> commen=
t at 2297 AND 2298. This suggests the old camera overlay was NOT deleted =
=E2=80=94 she pasted the new block but didn't remove the old one! OR: the o=
ld comment at 2297, then her new file (which itself begins with <code data-=
v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- =
CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code>) at 2298, followed by new HTML.</div><div clas=
s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But where's the OLD cam-wrap div? If the old H=
TML block was still there, line 2299 would be the OLD <code data-v-bfaabce6=
=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;div class=3D"c=
am-wrap" id=3D"cam-o"&gt;</code> with old children (old video etc.), and he=
r new div would appear after the old one ended. Here line 2299 immediately =
shows <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code=
-inline">&lt;div class=3D"cam-wrap" id=3D"cam-o"&gt;</code> followed by vid=
eo/canvas at 2300-2301, then <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"=
" class=3D"segment-code-inline">cam-top</code> with the new flip SVG (lines=
 2303-2305), <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segme=
nt-code-inline">cam-top-group</code>, flash button with <code data-v-bfaabc=
e6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&amp;#9889;</cod=
e> (new), close with X svg (new), multi-photo strip (new comment <code data=
-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!--=
 Multi-photo strip --&gt;</code>), capture-actions with the new buttons (Re=
take with =E2=86=A9 =E2=80=94 new).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">So this all looks like HER NEW file 2 content... but then what's at 229=
7? Another <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment=
-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code>? And 2295 <code data-v-b=
faabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;/div&gt=
;</code> =E2=80=94 end of the previous section (sidebar?).</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hold on. Maybe the old block WAS deleted and th=
is is clean: old CAMERA OVERLAY comment deleted, new one pasted. But then w=
hy TWO identical comments at 2297 and 2298?</div><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">Possibility: she deleted the old block's content but the old co=
mment line remained, then pasted file 2 (which starts with the comment) rig=
ht after it. That would leave a stray duplicate comment =E2=80=94 harmless!=
 Just a comment.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">OR possibility:=
 the old block is still fully there below/above and she inserted the new bl=
ock without deleting. If the old cam-wrap still exists, there would be TWO =
<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inlin=
e">&lt;div class=3D"cam-wrap" id=3D"cam-o"&gt;</code> elements =E2=80=94 th=
e second's duplicate IDs would break JS ($ returns first match). Need to ch=
eck!</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">From the screenshots: I see=
 only ONE cam-wrap visible starting at 2299. The old one would have had chi=
ldren in a different order (old HTML started: video, canvas, cam-flash, cam=
-c, cam-x, preview...). Here immediately after cam-wrap we see new-structur=
e content (cam-top with flip svg, cam-top-group). This matches file 2's beg=
inning exactly. So the old overlay appears deleted =E2=80=94 the stray dupl=
icate comment at 2297 is probably leftover from incomplete selection (she s=
elected starting AFTER the old comment line, or the delete left one comment=
 line).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait, actually =E2=80=94=
 could BOTH comments be from her paste? My file 2 content: <code data-v-bfa=
abce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMER=
A OVERLAY --&gt;\n&lt;div class=3D"cam-wrap"...</code> =E2=80=94 only ONE c=
omment. And it ends with blank lines then LIGHTBOX follows. The two comment=
s at 2297/2298: one old leftover + one new. So: old comment not deleted, bu=
t old CONTENT deleted? That doesn't make sense either =E2=80=94 if she sele=
cted from the comment line to LIGHTBOX and deleted, the comment would be go=
ne too.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">More likely: her selecti=
on started at the comment line of the OLD block but ended somewhere inside.=
.. ugh, can't fully tell. The safest interpretation from what I see: new bl=
ock is in place; there may be a duplicate stray comment (cosmetic) AND I ne=
ed to verify the old block is really gone and the new block ends correctly =
before LIGHTBOX.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The second scre=
enshot ends at line 2333 =E2=80=94 can't see the end of the camera overlay =
or LIGHTBOX. I need her to check: Ctrl+F <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">id=3D"cam-o"</code> =E2=80=94 c=
ount occurrences. If TWO =E2=86=92 old block still present =E2=86=92 proble=
m. If ONE =E2=86=92 clean, just remove stray duplicate comment (optional).<=
/div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also check the end: search <code=
 data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&l=
t;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> and confirm the new cam-wrap's closing <code d=
ata-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;=
/div&gt;</code> sits right before it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">So my reply: mostly great =E2=80=94 structure looks right, new skelet=
on visible; but I spot a possible stray duplicate comment and need two veri=
fication checks before file 3:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Ctrl+F <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" c=
lass=3D"segment-code-inline">id=3D"cam-o"</code> =E2=80=94 should find exac=
tly 1 (screenshot the count)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Scroll/search <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 confirm i=
t exists right after the camera block ends.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"pa=
ragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually GitHub editor find shows "x of y" matches. A=
sk her to search <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"s=
egment-code-inline">id=3D"cam-o"</code> and tell me the count. And search <=
code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline=
">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> exists. Quick.</div></div></div></div></di=
v> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"t=
rue"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"=
true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----></div=
><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__part toolcall-rollup__=
flat"><!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markd=
own-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto">Beautiful progress =E2=80=94 I can see the new skele=
ton: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-=
inline">cam-wrap</code>, the flip-camera SVG, the gold flash button, multi-=
photo strip, the Retake/Add/Done row. File 2's DNA is all there =F0=9F=91=
=8F</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But I spotted something that=
 needs a 10-second check before we move on: there are <strong>two</strong> =
<code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inlin=
e">&lt;!-- CAMERA OVERLAY --&gt;</code> comments stacked at lines 2297=E2=
=80=932298. Probably just a leftover scrap of the old comment =E2=80=94 <em=
>but</em> if the OLD camera block is also still lurking below, we'd have tw=
o cameras fighting over the same name, and that would break everything quie=
tly.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Two quick checks:</div><ol =
start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Press <strong>Ctrl+F<=
/strong>, type <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"seg=
ment-code-inline">id=3D"cam-o"</code> =E2=80=94 tell me how many matches it=
 shows (look for "1 of X" in the find box). We need exactly <strong>1</stro=
ng>.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Then search <code =
data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt=
;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 it should still exist (that's the lan=
dmark right after the camera).</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">If check 1 says <strong>1</strong> =E2=80=94 you're golden, just =
a harmless duplicate comment, and we roll on to file 3. If it says <strong>=
2</strong> =E2=80=94 stop, screenshot, and don't touch anything else. You'r=
e doing great, this is exactly why we check =F0=9F=94=8D=F0=9F=92=9B</div><=
/div></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail"=
><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><!----></div>=
