data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"resize-container" style=3D"height: 0px; opaci=
ty: 0;"><div data-v-b90066f2=3D"" class=3D"slot-container"><div data-v-048c=
b31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolcall-content=
-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">Main branch is INTACT =E2=80=94 it has the edit block (editi=
ngPostId between camera and profile), no v2 CSS yet (her edits uncommitted,=
 correct).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So HER EDITOR SESSION=
 swallowed the editingPostId/editPost/delPost/repost block. How? One of her=
 selections today ate it. Most likely suspect: the file-2 HTML paste select=
ion =E2=80=94 if her Shift+click at <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb=
31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code> overs=
hot? No, that region is HTML...</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=
Hmm wait =E2=80=94 actually, could it be the file-1 CSS paste? css region [=
CAMERA, PROFILE css marker) =E2=80=94 no, that's CSS area ~line 650.</div><=
div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually =E2=80=94 how did those JS li=
nes vanish if her selections were at lines 651/2300? THEY COULDN'T. Unless.=
.. the phone session! The phone froze mid-paste =E2=80=94 when she went bac=
k, "it went back to home page again." If the phone had auto-committed its p=
artial state at some point (she might have tapped commit before it froze =
=E2=80=94 "It went back to home page" could mean the commit went through an=
d redirected home!), then main would contain partial edits. But main is cle=
an (no v2, has edit-block). So no.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">Alternative explanation: the editor screenshot line numbers vs reality =
=E2=80=94 maybe the GitHub editor's find-jump showed her a STALE position, =
and lines 3784-3785 in her editor view are exactly as main has them... but =
main has editingPostId between them. UNLESS her selection for file 3 =E2=80=
=94 no, not done.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hold on, maybe=
 I'm misreading the screenshot. Zoom mentally: line 3785 could be <code dat=
a-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var ca=
mIsVideo=3Dfalse;</code> =E2=80=94 which in the original sits right before =
postCam! Look at the screenshot list again:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">3780 window.toggleFlash=3Dfunction()...
3781 window.camRecorder=3Dnull;window.camRecording=3Dfalse;window.camVideoC=
hunks=3D[];
3782 window.toggleVideo=3Dfunction(){var btn=3D$('cam-video-btn')...
3783 var camIsVideo=3Dfalse;
3784 window.postCam=3Dasync function(){...
3785 // =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D PROFIL=
E =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
3786 window.renderProfile=3Dasync function()...
3787 window.toggleProfileSong=3Dfunction()...</div><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto">Original main order (from my analysis): CAMERA block contains=
 openCam, closeCam, swCam, snap, retake, updatePhotoStrip, addAnotherPhoto,=
 retakeLastPhoto, finishCapture, toggleFlash, camRecorder/camRecording/camV=
ideoChunks, toggleVideo, camIsVideo, postCam =E2=80=94 then editingPostId, =
editPost, delPost, repost =E2=80=94 then PROFILE.</div><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">In the screenshot, postCam (3784) is followed directly by=
 PROFILE (3785). The editPost/delPost/repost lines ARE missing from her wor=
king copy.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So her working copy i=
s corrupted =E2=80=94 some selection+delete ate ~4,700 chars. When? Possibl=
y during the phone freeze (phantom keystrokes?) or an overshoot selection d=
uring file 2 (if the LIGHTBOX anchor search landed her in the wrong place =
=E2=80=94 e.g., there are TWO <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D=
"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code>? If LIGHTBO=
X comment appeared twice and she selected from CAMERA OVERLAY to a LATER LI=
GHTBOX... there's only one lightbox div though).</div><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm, actually here's a very plausible mechanism: during he=
r file-2 selection, she Ctrl+F'd <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code>, pressed=
 Enter =E2=80=94 cursor at lightbox line =E2=80=94 then Shift+Click at its =
start... that's only ~90 lines. No way it reached 3784.</div><div class=3D"=
paragraph" dir=3D"auto">OTHER mechanism =E2=80=94 the file-1 selection: she=
 searched <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-=
code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> =E2=80=94 there might be TWO matche=
s?? The editor find showed... If she selected from the CAMERA <strong>CSS</=
strong> marker (line 650) to the <strong><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFILE</code></st=
rong> CSS marker =E2=80=94 all in CSS. No.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">OK, whatever the cause =E2=80=94 the fix is the same and simple:=
 <strong>Cancel changes and redo the session.</strong> Main is clean; her t=
hree pastes are verified; redo takes ~10 minutes with the exact same instru=
ctions. Instruct: click "Cancel changes" (top-right), confirm, then redo fi=
les 1=E2=86=922=E2=86=923 in a fresh editor, then commit.</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Give her that instruction clearly. Reassure: no=
thing committed, repo safe, this is exactly why we verify before committing=
.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-=
fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-meas=
ure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div></div></div></di=
v></div> <!----> <!----></div></div></div></div> <div data-v-0a722276=3D"" =
class=3D"toolcall-rollup__tail is-open"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"=
toolcall-rollup__tail-in"><div data-v-0a722276=3D"" class=3D"toolcall-rollu=
p__tail-divider"></div> <!----> <div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=
=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markd=
own"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Good news and a plot twist, boss=
:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Your repo (m=
ain) is 100% intact</strong> =E2=80=94 the edit-post/delete/repost code is =
safely there, and none of today's changes are committed yet. Nothing broken=
 has shipped.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F=
 <strong>But your editor session glitched</strong> =E2=80=94 somewhere in t=
he paste dance, your working copy swallowed a block of JavaScript (the edit=
-post/delete/repost functions, right between postCam and PROFILE). I don't =
know which keystroke did it, and it doesn't matter =E2=80=94 because we cau=
ght it <em>before</em> committing. This is exactly why we screenshot and ve=
rify.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>The fix is clean a=
nd total:</strong> we're ditching this session and starting fresh. Nothing =
is lost =E2=80=94 main is pristine and your three files are ready to go aga=
in.</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Click <s=
trong>"Cancel changes"</strong> (top-right of the editor) =E2=86=92 confirm=
. This discards the glitched session and reloads the clean file from main.<=
/div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Re-open the editor: <a =
data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://github.com/mychainli=
nkCA/Mychainlink/edit/main/index.html" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopener"=
>https://github.com/mychainlinkCA/Mychainlink/edit/main/index.html</a></div=
></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Repeat the three pastes exa=
ctly as before =E2=80=94 file 1 (CSS: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048=
cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> =E2=86=
=92 before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment=
-code-inline">/* =3D=3D=3D PROFILE</code>), file 2 (HTML: <code data-v-bfaa=
bce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- CAMERA=
 OVERLAY --&gt;</code> =E2=86=92 before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-0=
48cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">&lt;!-- LIGHTBOX --&gt;</code>),=
 file 3 (JS: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segme=
nt-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D CAMERA</code> =E2=86=92 before <strong><code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" da=
ta-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;<=
/code></strong> =E2=80=94 yes, that landmark is correct and it EXISTS in th=
e clean file; it'll sit a few lines below postCam, before the PROFILE marke=
r).</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Before committing t=
his time, do the two verification searches: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data=
-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">id=3D"cam-o"</code> (should =
be <strong>1</strong> match) and <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;</code> (shoul=
d exist). Then commit.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>Ten minutes of redo, zero risk. And hey =E2=80=94 this is literally the sa=
me discipline that saved us yesterday with the header. Measure twice, cut o=
nce. Go ahead and hit Cancel =E2=80=94 I'm watching every step =F0=9F=9B=A1=
=EF=B8=8F=F0=9F=92=9B</div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <=
