1c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She's back=
 (it's now 12:22 PM =E2=80=94 she slept, and there's a "Submit domain trans=
fer - Spaceship" tab open, so the domain transfer is in progress!).</div><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The screenshots show the CURRENT editor=
 state. Interesting =E2=80=94 the timestamps say 12:22 PM and the editor sh=
ows the OLD camera JS (window.openCam with old code, toggleVideo, cam-video=
-btn references). So this looks like a FRESH session (Cancel was clicked an=
d changes discarded =E2=80=94 or this is a new edit session) =E2=80=94 the =
old JS is back, which is what we WANT as the starting point.</div><div clas=
s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 look at screenshot 4 (12.22.26)=
: lines 3770-3784 show the OLD camera JS (openCam with audio:false? shows "=
location.hostname!=3D=3D'localhost'" =E2=80=94 old), toggleVideo at 3782, c=
amIsVideo at 3783, postCam at 3784, then line 3785 BLANK, 3786 <code data-v=
-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D PROFILE =3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</code>, 3787 renderProfile=
...</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hold on =E2=80=94 still no e=
ditingPostId between postCam and PROFILE! Even in this fresh view. Hmm wait=
, but my API check of main confirmed editingPostId EXISTS between camera an=
d profile (pc &lt; pe &lt; pp). But the editor shows postCam =E2=86=92 (bla=
nk) =E2=86=92 PROFILE.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm, wait=
. Let me look at screenshot 4 again: 3784 postCam, 3785 blank, 3786 PROFILE=
. But API says main has <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" cla=
ss=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;</code> between them. C=
ONTRADICTION again!</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Unless... th=
e line wrapping! "No wrap" is OFF now? Look at screenshot 1: lines like 376=
8-3776 are fragments of long lines =E2=80=94 with horizontal scroll. In scr=
eenshot 4, each function is one line. postCam at 3784 is one huge line. If =
editingPostId were at 3785... but 3785 shows blank and 3786 PROFILE.</div><=
div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm wait =E2=80=94 maybe I'm wrong abo=
ut which file the API fetched. raw.githubusercontent.com serves the LATEST =
COMMITTED main. The API check at ~8:15 AM said editingPostId at 314253, PRO=
FILE at 318930 =E2=80=94 between them: editPost, delPost, repost. So main d=
efinitely has those.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But the edi=
tor view (fresh session) doesn't show them?? Unless this session ISN'T fres=
h =E2=80=94 maybe she clicked "Cancel" but the editor kept her changes? No =
=E2=80=94 Cancel discards. The old camera JS is visible (toggleVideo etc.) =
=E2=80=94 meaning v2 JS is NOT in this session, so file 3 was never pasted =
here. And the CSS/HTML? Can't tell from these screenshots (they're all at l=
ines ~3770).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So the mystery: doe=
s THIS session contain editingPostId or not? The visible evidence says NO (=
postCam =E2=86=92 blank =E2=86=92 PROFILE).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">OH WAIT. I bet I know what's happening!! The GitHub editor with=
 SOFT WRAP. In screenshot 4, check the toolbar =E2=80=94 can't see. In scre=
enshots 1-3, lines 3768-3784 show FRAGMENTS =E2=80=94 meaning soft wrap IS =
ON for those, and what I'm reading as separate line numbers are WRAPPED SEG=
MENTS of the same logical lines!! Look at screenshot 1: line 3768 "e)('a');=
b.style.boxShadow=3D'none'})..." then 3771 "}.style.display=3D'none';..." =
=E2=80=94 those are CONTINUATIONS. The line numbers jump 3768=E2=86=923771=
=E2=86=923772=E2=86=923774=E2=86=923775=E2=86=923776=E2=86=923777=E2=86=923=
779... with skipped numbers (3769, 3770, 3773, 3778, 3780, 3781...) shown a=
s the tiny partially-visible lines at left? Actually the left shows numbers=
 3768, then a small "1" fragment... hard to tell. But numbers skip =E2=80=
=94 3777 then 3779 (3778 missing/hidden), 3783 then 3784 (shown small?)...<=
/div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm, in screenshot 4 (the widest=
 view): 3768, 3769, 3770, 3771... consecutive numbers, each a full function=
 line. No wrap issues there: 3781 camRecorder, 3782 toggleVideo, 3783 camIs=
Video, 3784 postCam, 3785 blank, 3786 PROFILE. If soft wrap were on, postCa=
m would span multiple visual rows but ONE number. Here postCam =3D 3784 onl=
y, blank =3D 3785, PROFILE =3D 3786.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto">So in the CURRENT editor buffer, editingPostId/editPost/delPost/repost=
 are STILL missing?! But main has them (API verified at 8:15 AM).</div><div=
 class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">...unless this editor session was opened =
BEFORE I told her to cancel, i.e., these screenshots are from the OLD glitc=
hed session?? The tab title says "Editing Mychainlink/index.html". The scre=
enshots at 12:22 =E2=80=94 she says "help me find this" =E2=80=94 probably =
hunting for the editingPostId landmark for file 3 paste, and she can't find=
 it because it's MISSING from her (old, uncancelled) session.</div><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm wait =E2=80=94 did she actually click Can=
cel? She came back at 12:22 with "help me find this" =E2=80=94 she may have=
 resumed the old session without cancelling. The old session still has the =
glitch (missing edit block).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">I M=
UST verify the current buffer state vs main. I can't see her buffer. But th=
e key insight: if she DIDN'T cancel, the buffer =3D old glitched session (C=
SS v2 + HTML v2 + missing edit block). If she DID cancel and reopened, buff=
er =3D clean main (should have editingPostId).</div><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">The screenshots show old camera JS (no v2) =E2=80=94 file 3 =
never pasted in either case. Can't distinguish via these.</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Best move: have her click Cancel NOW if she has=
n't (safe either way =E2=80=94 if buffer is clean, cancel loses nothing sin=
ce nothing new pasted; if buffer is glitched, cancel fixes it). Then fresh =
editor will match main, and editingPostId will be findable.</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually =E2=80=94 careful: if she DID paste fi=
les 1-2 in THIS session (post-cancel), cancelling would lose them. Check: d=
oes her current buffer have v2 CSS? Ask her to Ctrl+F <code data-v-bfaabce6=
=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">CAMERA v2</code> =
=E2=80=94 if found, files 1-2 are in this session. Then we need to SAVE the=
 edit-block instead: simpler path =E2=80=94 paste the missing editPost/delP=
ost/repost block back (I can extract it from main and give it as a mini-fil=
e!), then do file 3 with the correct boundaries.</div><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">That's actually the cleanest fix either way: give her the =
missing block (4,677 chars) to paste back right after postCam, then file 3 =
boundary becomes <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"s=
egment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> =E2=86=92 before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;</code=
> as originally planned =E2=80=94 everything consistent.</div><div class=3D=
"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait, but if her buffer is missing those lines and=
 she pastes them back, plus file 3 =E2=80=94 done. If her buffer is clean (=
editingPostId present), the mini-file is unnecessary but harmless if she sk=
ips it. Let me make it conditional: Step 1: Ctrl+F <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D=
"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dn=
ull;</code> =E2=80=94 if FOUND: proceed to file 3 paste directly (landmark =
exists). If NOT found: paste the rescue file right after the postCam line (=
I'll give exact anchor: the blank line before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" da=
ta-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D PROFILE</code>), then proceed to fi=
le 3.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me prepare the rescue =
file: extract from main html: from <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb3=
1c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;</code> to j=
ust before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment=
-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D PROFILE</code> =E2=80=94 save as rescue file.</div><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">Also noticed in screenshot 1: tab "Submit domain transfer=
 - Spaceship" =E2=80=94 the domain transfer is underway! Nice =E2=80=94 ack=
nowledge that win briefly.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also =
I should double check the editor's line-view confusion: my instructions ref=
erence search anyway, so line numbers don't matter.</div><div class=3D"para=
