=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She's asking: give her the txt to add inside ca=
mera before PROFILE. That's the rescue file =E2=80=94 but wait, she says "i=
nside camera before =3D=3Dprofile". The rescue block (editingPostId, editPo=
st, delPost, repost) goes right before the PROFILE marker =E2=80=94 which i=
s technically between the camera section and the profile section. That's ex=
actly the rescue file.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But hold =
on =E2=80=94 if she adds the rescue block before PROFILE, then the camera s=
ection still has OLD JS (openCam, toggleVideo etc.) =E2=80=94 she still nee=
ds file 3 to replace the camera JS. Her message suggests she just wants to =
patch the missing block and maybe thinks that's it. I should give her the r=
escue text in the chat directly (she asked for the txt to add =E2=80=94 may=
be she can't easily download/open the file on her setup; paste it in chat).=
</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But CAREFUL: she says "inside c=
amera before =3D=3Dprofile" =E2=80=94 the rescue block starts with <code da=
ta-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var e=
ditingPostId=3Dnull;</code> and contains editPost/delPost/repost =E2=80=94 =
that's what goes before PROFILE.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>Then after that, she STILL needs file 3 (replace old camera JS with new). =
Sequence matters:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">Paste rescue before PROFILE marker.</div></li><li><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Then file 3: select from <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data=
-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D CAMERA</code> to just before <code dat=
a-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var ed=
itingPostId=3Dnull;</code> and replace with file 3.</div></li></ol><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually =E2=80=94 order matters! If she past=
es rescue first, then does file 3 selection (CAMERA marker =E2=86=92 editin=
gPostId), the selection now ends at the freshly pasted editingPostId =E2=80=
=94 perfect, the old camera JS gets replaced, rescue stays.</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Alternatively she could do file 3 first =E2=80=
=94 but then editingPostId landmark doesn't exist yet... wait it WOULD exis=
t after file 3 paste? No =E2=80=94 file 3 replaces up TO editingPostId, kee=
ping it. But the landmark doesn't exist BEFORE the file-3 selection... Actu=
ally in her current buffer, editingPostId is MISSING. So she can't select u=
p to it. So rescue FIRST, then file 3. That's the order I gave before.</div=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Now she asks for the txt directly. G=
ive her the rescue block in a code block in chat (it's ~4,700 chars / 3 lon=
g lines =E2=80=94 acceptable to paste in chat). Memory says "always give fu=
ll code" =E2=80=94 good.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Also re=
mind: after rescue paste, then file 3 paste (instructions repeated briefly)=
.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me print the rescue conten=
t to paste it here. I need the exact content =E2=80=94 fetch it again in ip=
ython and print (I have it saved to /mnt/agents/output/0-RESCUE-edit-post-b=
lock.txt). Print it so I can copy into the chat message verbatim. It might =
be long but fine.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-f=
ade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scrol=
l-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></div></div>=
