 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"au=
to">She's saying: "noo i'm literally on that file so i just need everything=
 after editpost" =E2=80=94 hmm. She's IN the file, on that spot. She wants.=
.. "everything after editpost"?</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=
Interpretation: She found <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" c=
lass=3D"segment-code-inline">window.editPost</code>? Or she's saying she on=
ly needs the part AFTER editPost? Wait =E2=80=94 "i just need everything af=
ter editpost" =E2=80=94 maybe her buffer DOES have editPost but the rest is=
 missing? Earlier the search for <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;</code> =E2=80=
=94 she never confirmed found/not found.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Alternative read: "i'm literally on that file" =3D she's already =
in the editor with the file open. "i just need everything after editpost" =
=3D she wants the text that comes after the editPost function =E2=80=94 i.e=
., maybe her buffer has <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" cla=
ss=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;window.editPost=3Dfunct=
ion(id){...</code> partially and is cut off mid-way? So she needs the remai=
nder of the block after editPost?</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
">Or simplest: she's at the right spot in the file and wants me to just giv=
e the remaining code (delPost, repost) to paste after editPost =E2=80=94 ma=
ybe her buffer has editPost but is missing delPost/repost?</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Earlier when I printed the rescue block, she ma=
y have looked at her file and found <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb=
31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">editPost</code> IS there. So the mis=
sing part might be only delPost + repost. "everything after editpost" =3D g=
ive me delPost and repost.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">But w=
ait =E2=80=94 if editingPostId line was missing, editPost would also be mis=
sing (same line!). In her earlier find, she searched <code data-v-bfaabce6=
=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=
=3Dnull;</code> and I told her to report found/not found =E2=80=94 she repl=
ied asking for the txt to add before PROFILE. So it was not found =E2=86=92=
 editPost missing too.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Now she s=
ays "i just need everything after editpost" =E2=80=94 confusing. Maybe she =
means: the rescue block I gave was long; she wants ONLY the part after edit=
Post? Maybe she already pasted something?</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">OR =E2=80=94 reading again: "noo i'm literally on that file" =E2=
=80=94 she's rejecting something I said? Maybe she means she's already ON t=
hat spot in the file (found the location), "so i just need everything after=
 editpost" =E2=80=94 hmm, she might be looking at her buffer where she can =
see <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-i=
nline">editPost</code> exists and the file continues but she thinks somethi=
ng after it is missing?</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">I can't =
resolve the ambiguity from here. Best: give her the split version =E2=80=94=
 the block in two parts: (1) starts at <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-04=
8cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">var editingPostId=3Dnull;window.e=
ditPost=3D...</code> ends before <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">window.delPost</code>, and (2) delPost =
+ repost. And ask her to check what her file already has: does she see <cod=
e data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">w=
indow.editPost</code>? If yes, where does it stop?</div><div class=3D"parag=
raph" dir=3D"auto">Simplest useful action: give her the code AFTER editPost=
 =E2=80=94 i.e., from <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">window.delPost</code> through repost. That's "ever=
ything after editPost". If her buffer has everything up through editPost (m=
eaning her buffer actually contains the whole beginning but is missing delP=
ost/repost?), this fills it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Act=
ually here's a cleaner hypothesis!! Her buffer might have editPost (she can=
 see it) but be missing delPost/repost =E2=80=94 because the glitch swallow=
ed only part. The 12:22 screenshots couldn't confirm either way. So "everyt=
hing after editpost" =3D delPost + repost. Give exactly that.</div><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">From the rescue block: everything from <code =
data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">win=
dow.delPost=3Dfunction(id){...</code> to the end.</div><div class=3D"paragr=
aph" dir=3D"auto">Give that in a code block, short instructions: paste it r=
ight after the editPost line, before the PROFILE marker.</div></div></div><=
/div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hi=
