cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">She say=
s "ill merge to main" =E2=80=94 she wants to commit on the patch-2 branch a=
nd merge to main. That's the risky path I just warned against. I need to ex=
plain clearly why that's dangerous: the branch is based on an old snapshot =
=E2=80=94 merging would likely cause conflicts, and if merged via "theirs" =
or resolved sloppily, could erase main's newer work. GitHub will show merge=
 conflicts (there's already a "Resolve Conflicts" tab open =E2=80=94 sugges=
ting a conflict state exists).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">I=
 should firmly but kindly steer her away. The stakes: losing the Sept 12-14=
 work (terms gate, header restore, DM fixes, etc.). The alternative is 10 m=
inutes of pastes on main.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Be dir=
ect: "Boss, no =E2=80=94 I need to veto this one." As her advisor I should =
be clear. Explain: merge conflicts are already showing (Resolve Conflicts t=
ab), the branch is old, resolving 4000-line conflicts by hand is exactly ho=
w code dies. The clean path is faster and safer.</div><div class=3D"paragra=
ph" dir=3D"auto">Also =E2=80=94 her pattern: she tends to push through. I m=
ust be unambiguous but warm. Give her the direct comparison:</div><div clas=
s=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Merge path: commit on patch-2 =E2=86=92 PR =E2=
=86=92 CONFLICTS (because main moved on) =E2=86=92 resolve 4000-line file c=
onflicts by hand =E2=86=92 high chance of losing code =E2=86=92 possible si=
te breakage, again.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Clean path: =
Cancel =E2=86=92 edit main =E2=86=92 3 pastes (she's practiced) =E2=86=92 c=
ommit =E2=86=92 Build. ~10 min, zero conflicts, zero risk.</div><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Veto with love. Also note: even if merge resolv=
ed by taking "her version," that version =3D old base + camera edits =E2=80=
=94 missing terms gate and other newer features. I can prove it: fetch the =
patch-2 branch's index.html and diff against main to SHOW her what's missin=
g. That's compelling evidence. Let me do that quickly =E2=80=94 fetch branc=
h file and compare markers: terms gate (acceptTos), Sept 12 features, editi=
ngPostId, etc.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me fetch: <a =
data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://raw.githubuserconten=
t.com/mychainlinkCA/Mychainlink/mychainlinkCA-patch-2/index.html" rel=3D"no=
referrer nofollow noopener">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mychainlinkCA=
/Mychainlink/mychainlinkCA-patch-2/index.html</a> and check for key markers=
: 'acceptTos', 'TERMS_VERSION', 'm-tos', 'showTosGate', 'supabaseOnline', e=
tc. Also file size vs main.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scr=
oll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div clas=
s=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div></=
