data-v-048cb31c=3D"" data-v-9019dc97=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container toolc=
all-content-text"><div data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=
=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Fascinating! The comparison shows the OPPOSITE =
of what I feared:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"=
auto">patch-2 branch HAS <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" cl=
ass=3D"segment-code-inline">window.toggleProfileSong</code> (profile songs)=
 =E2=80=94 main does NOT!</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">patch-2 is SMALLER (409,150) than main (413,932) =E2=80=94 main is BIGGE=
R.</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So main is MISSING =
the profile-songs feature that the branch has! And the branch is missing ~4=
,800 chars of something that main has.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D=
"auto">So the branch isn't simply "older" =E2=80=94 the histories DIVERGED:=
 patch-2 has profile songs; main has something else extra (~4.8KB). What do=
es main have that branch lacks? Let me diff markers more. Interesting: earl=
ier her 12:22 buffer (on patch-2) was missing the edit block =E2=80=94 but =
the BRANCH file has editingPostId =E2=9C=85... her BUFFER edits =E2=89=A0 b=
ranch state (uncommitted). The branch base actually HAS editingPostId. So o=
n the branch, her paste of the rescue "after editingPostId" may have create=
d DUPLICATES in her buffer! Ugh.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>Wait =E2=80=94 but hold on: if the branch HAS everything and main lacks on=
ly profile-songs... what does MAIN have that the branch lacks (4.8KB)? Let =
me find out =E2=80=94 check distinctive markers from recent main commits: t=
he header restore is in both presumably. Main commits: e189ae5 (terms gate =
+ OAuth/profile saves), 6cc2f13 (TERMS_VERSION), b272735 (broke), 4e55da2 (=
header restore), e512226 (Go file), PR#8 merge.</div><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Let me diff more carefully =E2=80=94 find which functions e=
xist in main but not branch. Check: 'showTosGate', 'checkTextModeration', '=
checkImageModeration', 'renderThreadLocalMsgs', 'sendMediaMsg', 'sb.from('p=
osts')', 'data-deletion', 'openLiveModal'...</div><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Actually =E2=80=94 the right move now is different. She's wait=
ing. The situation: two diverged versions, each with something the other la=
cks:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Branch =
(patch-2): + profile songs, (and her uncommitted v2 camera pastes sit on to=
p)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Main: + ~4.8KB of ot=
her stuff (unknown =E2=80=94 possibly the Sept 12 DM/terms fixes, since pat=
ch-2 was created BEFORE those? but branch shows terms gate =E2=9C=85... hmm=
 confusing)</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Honestly t=
he cleanest path remains: main + 3 pastes. But wait =E2=80=94 now there's a=
 NEW consideration: main LACKS profile songs?! If main lacks toggleProfileS=
ong/renderProfile etc., then main is missing a feature that... the LIVE SIT=
E has? The live site (mychainlink.ca) renders =E2=80=94 and earlier her scr=
eenshots of the app... did profile songs exist on the live site? She tested=
 the app Sept 13-14 =E2=80=94 profile song feature came from one of the Cla=
w commits (Sept 12: "Add Supabase Storage policies + fix moderation/spam/re=
port flows + bump SW"... hmm, or another). If main lacks it, the live site =
lacks it (site builds from main!).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"aut=
o">Wait =E2=80=94 actually let me recheck: does main REALLY lack profile so=
ngs? The marker 'window.toggleProfileSong' returned =E2=9D=8C for main. Hmm=
 =E2=80=94 but wait, earlier I checked main multiple times today and extrac=
ted the PROFILE block FROM MAIN including 'window.toggleProfileSong' =E2=80=
=94 the rescue profile block I extracted contained it! Let me re-verify... =
In my profile-block extraction I printed the block and it included togglePr=
ofileSong etc. And that extraction came FROM main. So main HAS profile song=
s =E2=80=94 but my marker check just said =E2=9D=8C?!</div><div class=3D"pa=
ragraph" dir=3D"auto">The check: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=
=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">'window.toggleProfileSong' in mainf</co=
de> =E2=86=92 False. But the extracted profile block from main contained <c=
ode data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline"=
>window.toggleProfileSong=3Dfunction</code> =E2=80=94 I saw it in the rescu=
e block print? Let me recall the rescue profile block print... I printed fi=
rst 180 chars: <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"seg=
ment-code-inline">// =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D PROFILE =3D=3D=3D...\nwindow.renderProfile=3Dasync function(){...</c=
ode> and last 160. I didn't verify toggleProfileSong explicitly in main. Bu=
t in the earlier "checks" run (after her commit) =E2=80=94 'toggleProfileSo=
ng': 'window.toggleProfileSong=3Dfunction' in cur =E2=86=92 that printed =
=E2=9C=85! That check ran on main at ~13:10. So main HAD toggleProfileSong =
at 13:10!</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Now this run says main=
 =E2=9D=8C?? Something changed on main between 13:10 and 14:27?! Did she co=
mmit/merge something in the last hour?! She was on patch-2... The "Resolve =
Conflicts" tab was open... Did she MERGE patch-2 into main at some point?!<=
/div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">OH NO. Or =E2=80=94 wait, maybe =
my mainf fetch failed partially? mainf size 413,932. At 13:10 the size was =
416,047. Different! Main CHANGED since 13:10 =E2=80=94 it SHRANK by ~2,100 =
chars. So she DID something to main in the last hour =E2=80=94 possibly mer=
ged a branch or committed the patch-2 buffer!</div><div class=3D"paragraph"=
 dir=3D"auto">Hmm wait, actually at 13:06-13:10 the Go PR #8 merged. The 41=
6,047 check was at ~13:10 AFTER that merge. Now main =3D 413,932. So main c=
hanged AGAIN after 13:10. She's been busy. Maybe she merged patch-2 (with t=
he conflict resolution!) =E2=80=94 the "Resolve Conflicts" tab! If she reso=
lved conflicts by picking patch-2's version for chunks, main could have LOS=
T things (like profile songs?? no wait =E2=80=94 patch-2 HAS profile songs =
and main NOW lacks them =E2=86=92 consistent with "merge took branch side"!=
).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So current main =3D post-merg=
e state: lost profile songs (and possibly other things), gained her v2 came=
ra (if her buffer commits went in). This is getting messy. I need to check =
what main currently has: v2 camera? profile songs? Let me run a fuller diag=
nostic on the CURRENT main: v2 markers, terms gate, profile section, file s=
ize, and recent commits.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Then de=
cide the recovery: what's missing must be restored. My local copies: I have=
 the rescue profile block saved (toggleProfileSong, saveProfileSong, delete=
ProfileSong, renderProfile) =E2=80=94 extracted from the GOOD main at ~13:1=
0. If current main lost the whole PROFILE section, I can give her a restore=
 block.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Run diagnostics now: che=
ck current main for: CAMERA v2, setCamMode, renderProfile, toggleProfileSon=
g, PROFILE marker, acceptTos, file size, and fetch recent commits.</div></d=
iv></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-botto=
m" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentin=
