 OLD one (no "v2"). But JS shows v2 present and toggleVideo gone.</div><div=
 class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">So main has: OLD CSS + (HTML?) + v2 JS?? =
That means SHE COMMITTED SOMETHING! The patch-2 branch got merged?! Remembe=
r the "Resolve Conflicts - Pull Re..." tab. She said "ill merge to main" =
=E2=80=94 and I vetoed... but maybe before/after my veto, the merge went th=
rough!</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Evidence: earlier check a=
t 13:11 (my "Go check my code" verification) showed main WITHOUT v2 (toggle=
Video present, no setCamMode). Now (14:35+) main HAS v2 JS but seemingly OL=
D CSS. So between 13:11 and 14:30, a commit/merge landed on main that repla=
ced the JS (and maybe HTML) with v2 but kept old CSS??</div><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto">That's a mixed state =E2=80=94 exactly the kind of F=
rankenstein I warned about. If old CSS + new HTML/JS is live: the new HTML =
uses classes that old CSS doesn't style =E2=86=92 broken-looking camera (in=
visible elements, wrong layout). And the site might be partially broken NOW=
 (she may have hit Build?).</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let =
me check the full state of main thoroughly:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div c=
lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">CSS: v2 marker present? (<code data-v-bfaab=
