1c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The kernel=
 restarted =E2=80=94 /mnt/agents/output/index.html is gone (the sandbox fil=
esystem reset, or the kernel env reset wiped output?). The og-image.png I j=
ust saved =E2=80=94 did it survive? The banner save succeeded in the previo=
us cell, same session... but if the FS is shared, og-image.png might be the=
re. The error says index.html missing =E2=80=94 so the output dir was wiped=
 (kernel restart cleared /mnt/agents/output? or the file was never written =
there... it WAS written and delivered earlier). Either way: I must REBUILD =
the entire index.html from scratch now: fetch known-good base (4e55da2e49),=
 apply v2 CSS/HTML/JS, favicon bump, OG tags (with new tagline), and ALSO r=
e-insert the PROFILE rescue block (since base is pre-merge known-good, it H=
AS the profile section =E2=80=94 no rescue needed!).</div><div class=3D"par=
agraph" dir=3D"auto">Wait =E2=80=94 the known-good commit 4e55da2e49 predat=
es the merge and HAS the profile section. Building from it avoids the missi=
ng-profile problem entirely. Then the assembled file is complete: v2 camera=
, favicon v4, OG tags with new tagline, profile section intact. The rescue =
paste step becomes unnecessary!</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">=
Also NEW_CSS/NEW_HTML/NEW_JS files =E2=80=94 are they still on disk? The ou=
tput dir seems wiped... check: read the three files; if gone, I have their =
content... I don't have them in memory anymore (kernel reset). Ugh. The wid=
get HTML had mockup code, not the files. Can I reconstruct? The three files=
 were written from variables defined in earlier cells =E2=80=94 lost with t=
he kernel.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Options:</div><ol sta=
rt=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Check if /mnt/agents/out=
put files survive (only index.html missing? or all?). og-image.png was just=
 written =E2=80=94 test existence.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" d=
ir=3D"auto">If the three v2 files are gone, rebuild NEW_CSS/NEW_HTML/NEW_JS=
 from scratch =E2=80=94 I wrote them once; I can rewrite (long, but doable.=
.. it'd be a big effort and risk of divergence from what she may have parti=
ally used. BUT actually the merged main ALREADY contains v2 JS =E2=80=94 I =
could extract v2 pieces from current main? The current main has v2 JS (with=
 the slash bug) and old CSS/HTML. So: base =3D known-good 4e55da2e49 (has o=
ld CSS/HTML + profile intact + editingPostId intact). From current main, ex=
tract: NEW_CSS? No =E2=80=94 current main CSS is OLD. Only v2 JS exists in =
current main. So CSS+HTML must be rebuilt from scratch.</div></li></ol><div=
 class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Hmm wait =E2=80=94 actually check output =
dir first. Maybe only index.html vanished because... actually the delivered=
 REF files: og-image.png was delivered earlier too and I just overwrote it.=
 The rescue file + 1/2/3 files were delivered earlier =E2=80=94 if the whol=
e output dir was wiped, all gone.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
">Let me check the filesystem in one cell and decide. If the 3 files surviv=
e, rebuild index.html quickly (I have all pieces). If not, I must rewrite C=
SS/HTML files fresh (long code, but I can reproduce =E2=80=94 I have full k=
nowledge of what I wrote; the HTML I can reconstruct exactly; CSS too; JS c=
an be harvested from current main fixing the slash!).</div><div class=3D"pa=
ragraph" dir=3D"auto">Actually smartest: for the JS, fetch current main and=
 extract its v2 JS block (fixing leading <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-=
048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">/</code> =E2=86=92 <code data-v=
-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">//</code>=
) =E2=80=94 no need to retype. For CSS/HTML, retype from my original messag=
e content (I have it in conversation history =E2=80=94 files 1 &amp; 2 cont=
ent was generated by me; I can reproduce identical or near-identical conten=
t; I remember the structure precisely since I authored it this session).</d=
iv><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Plan in ONE cell: check dir; if pa=
rts exist use them; else reconstruct; assemble; validate; write index.html =
+ og files. Keep it efficient.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"=
scroll-edge-fade scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div c=
lass=3D"scroll-edge-fade-measure-sentinel" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div></div=
></div></div></div></div></div></div> <!----> <!----><!----> <div data-v-04=
8cb31c=3D"" data-v-8fac2c49=3D"" class=3D"markdown-container"><div data-v-0=
48cb31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The s=
